                        <div class="col-sm-12 col-md-6 col-lg-4">

                            <div class="card job-card mb-3 mb-md-6"
                                data-country="IN"
                                data-title="Business Analyst">
                                
                                <div class="card-body d-flex flex-column">

                                    <h5 class="card-title">
                                        <a
                                            href="https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com/osttrahcm/CANDIDATEPORTAL/jobs/1226"
                                            class="job-title-link" target="_blank">
                                            Business Analyst                                        </a>
                                    </h5>

                                    <p class="job-location text-muted mb-2">
                                        Gurugram, HR, IN                                    </p>

                                                                            <div class="job-description mb-0">
                                                                                                                                        <section class="job-section mb-4">
                                                    <h6 class="mb-2" style="font-weight: 600;">Overview</h6>
                                                    <p>Job Overview</p><p>About the Role:</p><p>The team: Our Engineering team develops and maintains modern, cloud-based applications and AI-powered solutions that support global business operations. Team members collaborate across Product, Architecture, QA, and DevOps functions to build reliable, secure, and scalable solutions. The team embraces agile delivery practices and encourages continuous learning, innovation, and professional growth.</p><p>Responsibilities and impact:</p><p>We build a platform that replaces manual month-end NAV reconciliation and investor income allocation processes for hedge fund operations teams. You will be the bridge between our fund clients and our engineering team — understanding how each client&#039;s fund accounting operations work, translating that into precise specifications, and ensuring the platform delivers correct financial outcomes. This is a client-facing role.</p>                                                </section>
                                                                                            <section class="job-section mb-4">
                                                    <h6 class="mb-2" style="font-weight: 600;">Responsibilities</h6>
                                                    <ul><li>Lead UAT and Stakeholder Engagement: Collaborate directly with fund operations teams during month-end to observe reconciliation and allocation workflows, conduct feature demonstrations, and drive user acceptance testing (UAT).</li><li>Own End-to-End Validation: Manage the full feature delivery lifecycle, ensuring that calculation results are fully verified and confirmed as accurate by the client before deeming a feature complete.</li><li>Drive Hands-on Analysis: Act as a forward-deployed business analyst by drafting comprehensive specifications, exploring complex calculation edge cases, and proactively contributing to technical solutions.</li><li>Collaborate with Engineering: Partner closely with engineering teams to define and refine data models and calculation logic, ensuring business requirements translate into robust technical implementations.</li><li>Execute Technical Validation: Perform hands-on data validation and analysis by utilizing SQL and other technical tools to verify system outputs and ensure data integrity.</li><li>Integrate AI-Augmented Workflows: Leverage AI assistants to accelerate analysis and process efficiency, maintaining a curiosity-driven approach to pushing the boundaries of what is possible with new technology.</li></ul>                                                </section>
                                                                                            <section class="job-section mb-4">
                                                    <h6 class="mb-2" style="font-weight: 600;">Requirements</h6>
                                                    <p>You will have 5-8 years of experience with fluency in fund accounting: NAV calculation, trial balances, portfolio valuations, realized vs. unrealized P&amp;L, management and performance fee waterfalls, hurdle rates, high water marks, investor allocations, capital activity processing (subscriptions, redemptions, transfers), equalisation mechanics, and accounting period controls.</p><p>Required Skills</p><ul><li>Domain Expertise and Accounting Rigor: Deep knowledge of fund accounting and administration systems, utilizing strong analytical and problem-solving skills to break down complex scenarios, identify edge cases, and maintain absolute precision in calculations to prevent compounding errors across periods.</li><li>Business Analysis and Delivery: Proven proficiency in requirements elicitation—including structured interviews, process flows, and defining acceptance criteria—combined with a proactive, ownership-driven mindset to drive deliverables to completion without needing prompting.</li><li>Client Relations and Results Focus: Exceptional client-facing confidence in presenting methodologies and fielding difficult questions when results deviate, with an outcome-driven mindset that measures success strictly by the accuracy of financial results rather than completed process steps.</li><li>Technical Acumen and AI Integration: Strong technical literacy, including SQL for data analysis and validation, paired with a genuine appetite for integrating and utilizing AI-augmented workflows daily to accelerate work and contribute directly to technical solutions.</li></ul><p>Preferred Skills</p><ul><li>Fund Accounting &amp; Operations Expertise: Deep functional expertise in fund accounting operations, encompassing complex fee calculation methodologies (management fee accrual, incentive fees with hurdle and HWM, equalisation, crystallisation, series/lot accounting), investor reporting, capital activity workflows, multi-currency fund structures, and comprehensive reconciliation workflows, including managing tolerance thresholds, variance investigation, and resolution processes.</li><li>AI-Augmented Technical Skills: Demonstrated hands-on practical experience utilizing AI assistants (e.g., Copilot, ChatGPT) as essential tools to accelerate and optimize professional workflows, specifically applying them to complex financial analysis, specification writing, and data exploration tasks.</li></ul><p>The location: Gurgaon,India</p><p>Our Benefits: Global vision, local impact</p><p>At OSTTRA, our benefits philosophy offers a market-competitive package that reflects our position as an industry leader. We want to ensure you feel valued, secure, and empowered wherever you are in the world.</p><p>Our approach is built on three core pillars:</p><ul><li>Global foundations: We provide a baseline of excellence across all our offices, focusing on comprehensive Health &amp; Wellness, Financial Security, and Work-Life Balance. No matter your location, you are part of a culture that prioritizes your holistic well-being.</li><li>Locally tailored: We benchmark in each market to ensure our packages are genuinely competitive where you live and work.</li><li>Flexibility and growth: We empower you to work in a way that suits your life. This includes a hybrid working model, generous leave policies, and a commitment to your continuous professional development.</li></ul><p>The Trust employee ownership plan</p><p>Every employee at OSTTRA is an owner, and a member of The Trust, our employee ownership programme. Our distinct culture encourages colleagues to think and act like owners and raise the bar constantly. This plan reflects our belief that when we work together to build a stronger, more valuable organisation, then all colleagues should benefit from the value we create.</p><p>About OSTTRA</p><p>We build and operate the infrastructure that the world’s post-trade financial system runs on. Launched in 2021, we have unified more than 20 years of heritage and expertise from four industry leaders into a single, integrated business.</p><p>Today,we operate a trusted network that connects thousands of market participants to streamline end-to-end workflows, from trade capture through portfolio optimisation.We translate industry change into workable process, engineering an open, intelligent ecosystem that removes friction and reduces risk for the global markets.</p><p>Our distinct ownership culture is underpinned by four behaviours: boldness, curiosity, accountability, and collaboration. In 2025 we were acquired by KKR, one of the world’s most successful private equity firms, and are on a journey of growth and impact.</p><p>Joining our team now is a unique opportunity - you will help to shape the next generation of post-trade, transform shared infrastructure into shared benefit, and accelerate your own career. Learn more atwww.osttra.com.</p><p>Equal opportunity employer statement at OSTTRA</p><p>We are committed to fostering a connected and engaged workplace where all colleagues have access to opportunities based on their skills, experience, and contributions. Our hiring practices emphasise fairness, transparency, and merit, ensuring that we attract and retain the best talent. By valuing different perspectives and promoting a culture of respect and collaboration, we drive and operate the infrastructure that the world’s post-trade financial system runs on.</p>                                                </section>
                                                                                    </div>
