                        <div class="col-sm-12 col-md-6 col-lg-4">

                            <div class="card job-card mb-3 mb-md-6"
                                data-country="IN"
                                data-title="Sr Product Analysis &amp; Design Specialist">
                                
                                <div class="card-body d-flex flex-column">

                                    <h5 class="card-title">
                                        <a
                                            href="https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com/osttrahcm/CANDIDATEPORTAL/jobs/1238"
                                            class="job-title-link" target="_blank">
                                            Sr Product Analysis &amp; Design Specialist                                        </a>
                                    </h5>

                                    <p class="job-location text-muted mb-2">
                                        Gurugram, HR, IN                                    </p>

                                                                            <div class="job-description mb-0">
                                                                                                                                        <section class="job-section mb-4">
                                                    <h6 class="mb-2" style="font-weight: 600;">Overview</h6>
                                                    <p>Job Overview</p><p>About the Role:</p><p>The team: The OSTTRA Product team comprises Capital Markets professionals dedicated to designing, building, and safeguarding the applications that power our network. Leveraging contemporary microservices and cloud-based architectures, we manage a sophisticated landscape of high-performance, compute-intensive technology.</p><p>Responsibilities and impact:</p><p>OSTTRA is currently seeking a Technical Product Manager to support our FX &amp; Securities Platforms, ensuring seamless trade processing, regulatory compliance, and settlement across systems that handle over 100 million messages daily.</p><p>In this role, you will collaborate with agile cross-functional teams—including product, development, QA, and operations—across global locations like India, Singapore, Tokyo, New York, and London. The ideal candidate brings strong analytical, organizational, and communication skills, a process-oriented mindset, and the ability to build robust internal and external relationships with clients, clearing houses, venues, and trade repositories in a fast-paced environment.</p>                                                </section>
                                                                                            <section class="job-section mb-4">
                                                    <h6 class="mb-2" style="font-weight: 600;">Responsibilities</h6>
                                                    <ul><li>Coordination with stakeholders for requirements elicitation to meet customer/market expectations</li><li>Ensure alignment among the business, tech and other teams</li><li>Prioritization of future features and functionalities, to create product roadmap</li><li>Coordinate and communicate the product roadmap with all stakeholders and ensure its delivery</li><li>Analyze and represent the requirements in epics/stories, usecases, and define acceptance criteria for each functionality towards delivery</li><li>Support other teams in analysing production issues, client queries</li><li>Support UAT (internal and client teams) from functional point of view and incorporate feedback in future releases of OTC &amp; ETD derivatives terms and principles</li></ul>                                                </section>
                                                                                            <section class="job-section mb-4">
                                                    <h6 class="mb-2" style="font-weight: 600;">Requirements</h6>
                                                    <p>Fundamental requirement:</p><ul><li>Post graduate – Bachelor’s or Master’s Degree preferred in related field</li><li>7+ years of relevant professional experience</li><li>Demonstrate experience of working in a product management environment</li><li>Strong Analytical &amp; Communication skills</li><li>Good knowledge of requirements elicitation, structured analysis, requirement documentation, stakeholder management, use case and user story definition and other business analysis techniques</li><li>Commercial awareness and financial services experience</li></ul><p>Additional preferred requirements:</p><ul><li>Understanding of OTC &amp; ETD derivatives terms and principles</li><li>Experience working as a business analyst in an agile scrum team</li><li>Familiarity with financials asset classes and trading lifecycle</li><li>Understanding of FIX/FpML or other messaging formats or protocols</li><li>Commercial awareness and financial services experience</li></ul><p>The location: Gurgaon,India</p><p>Our Benefits: Global vision, local impact</p><p>At OSTTRA, our benefits philosophy offers a market-competitive package that reflects our position as an industry leader. We want to ensure you feel valued, secure, and empowered wherever you are in the world.</p><p>Our approach is built on three core pillars:</p><ul><li>Global foundations: We provide a baseline of excellence across all our offices, focusing on comprehensive Health &amp; Wellness, Financial Security, and Work-Life Balance. No matter your location, you are part of a culture that prioritizes your holistic well-being.</li><li>Locally tailored: We benchmark in each market to ensure our packages are genuinely competitive where you live and work.</li><li>Flexibility and growth: We empower you to work in a way that suits your life. This includes a hybrid working model, generous leave policies, and a commitment to your continuous professional development.</li></ul><p>The Trust employee ownership plan</p><p>Every employee at OSTTRA is an owner, and a member of The Trust, our employee ownership programme. Our distinct culture encourages colleagues to think and act like owners and raise the bar constantly. This plan reflects our belief that when we work together to build a stronger, more valuable organisation, then all colleagues should benefit from the value we create.</p><p>About OSTTRA</p><p>We build and operate the infrastructure that the world’s post-trade financial system runs on. Launched in 2021, we have unified more than 20 years of heritage and expertise from four industry leaders into a single, integrated business.</p><p>Today,we operate a trusted network that connects thousands of market participants to streamline end-to-end workflows, from trade capture through portfolio optimisation.We translate industry change into workable process, engineering an open, intelligent ecosystem that removes friction and reduces risk for the global markets.</p><p>Our distinct ownership culture is underpinned by four behaviours: boldness, curiosity, accountability, and collaboration. In 2025 we were acquired by KKR, one of the world’s most successful private equity firms, and are on a journey of growth and impact.</p><p>Joining our team now is a unique opportunity - you will help to shape the next generation of post-trade, transform shared infrastructure into shared benefit, and accelerate your own career. Learn more atwww.osttra.com.</p><p>Equal opportunity employer statement at OSTTRA</p><p>We are committed to fostering a connected and engaged workplace where all colleagues have access to opportunities based on their skills, experience, and contributions. Our hiring practices emphasise fairness, transparency, and merit, ensuring that we attract and retain the best talent. By valuing different perspectives and promoting a culture of respect and collaboration, we drive and operate the infrastructure that the world’s post-trade financial system runs on.</p>                                                </section>
