                <!-- Expose data for client-side filtering -->
                <script>
                    window.DayforceJobs = [{"Title":"Experienced Software Engineer","Description":"Job Overview\n\n\nThe team:\nThe development team is based in Stockholm. It consists of highly skilled and helpful individuals with diverse backgrounds, each engineer playing a unique part in serving our global customer base. We value learning from and supporting each other in order to benefit from our different strengths and experiences. We are strong believers that collaboration is key to innovation and to produce a user experience and a technical solution that we can be proud of.\n\nResponsibilities and impact:\nOSTTRA is a FinTech company at the heart of the global financial system, dedicated to building the future of post-trade processing. Our products within the Trade Lifecycle division cover many of these areas, such as portfolio reconciliation, risk calculations, collateral management, and settlement automation. Improving these systems has a real impact on reducing the systemic risk of the global financial market while boosting operational efficiency and producing cost savings for many of the largest banks in the world.\n\nAs an experienced software engineer, you are responsible for:\n   \u2022 Actively contribute to the development and architecture of the system to meet new and changing business needs\n   \u2022 Design and evaluate new architecture principles\n   \u2022 Continuously look for opportunities to improve our tools and our ways of working\n   \u2022 Be part of the team taking care of the overall system health\n   \u2022 Mentoring of colleagues\n   \u2022 Represent the team in company-wide initiative\nWhat we\u2019re looking for:\nFundamental requirement:\n   \u2022 More than 10 years of relevant experience\n   \u2022 Excellent communication skills\n   \u2022 Demonstrated ability to drive bigger initiatives independently and with the team\n   \u2022 An aptitude and willingness to improve yourself, others around you, and our ways of working\n   \u2022 Someone who will work from the office at least 3 days per week\n Additional preferred requirements:\n   \u2022 An interest in financial markets\nThe location: Stockholm, Sweden\nRight to work requirements:\nThis role is limited to persons with indefinite right to work in Sweden.\n\n\nOur Benefits: Global vision, local impact\nAt OSTTRA, our benefits philosophy offers a market-competitive package that reflects our position as an industry leader. We want to ensure you feel valued, secure, and empowered wherever you are in the world.\nOur approach is built on three core pillars:\n   \u2022 Global foundations: We provide a baseline of excellence across all our offices, focusing on comprehensive Health & Wellness, Financial Security, and Work-Life Balance. No matter your location, you are part of a culture that prioritizes your holistic well-being.\n   \u2022 Locally tailored: We benchmark in each market to ensure our packages are genuinely competitive where you live and work.\n   \u2022 Flexibility and growth: We empower you to work in a way that suits your life. This includes a hybrid working model, generous leave policies, and a commitment to your continuous professional development.\n\nThe Trust employee ownership plan\nEvery employee at OSTTRA is an owner, and a member of The Trust, our employee ownership programme. Our distinct culture encourages colleagues to think and act like owners and raise the bar constantly.\nThis plan reflects our belief that when we work together to build a stronger, more valuable organisation, then all colleagues should benefit from the value we create.\nAbout OSTTRA\nWe build and operate the infrastructure that the world\u2019s post-trade financial system runs on. Launched in 2021, we have unified more than 20 years of heritage and expertise from four industry leaders into a single, integrated business.\nToday,we operate a trusted network that connects thousands of market participants to streamline end-to-end workflows, from trade capture through portfolio optimisation.We translate industry change into workable process, engineering an open, intelligent ecosystem that removes friction and reduces risk for the global markets.\n\nOur distinct ownership culture is underpinned by four behaviours: boldness, curiosity, accountability, and collaboration. In 2025 we were acquired by KKR, one of the world\u2019s most successful private equity firms, and are on a journey of growth and impact.\nJoining our team now is a unique opportunity - you will help to shape the next generation of post-trade, transform shared infrastructure into shared benefit, and accelerate your own career. Learn more at www.osttra.com.\nEqual opportunity employer statement at OSTTRA:\nWe are committed to fostering a connected and engaged workplace where all colleagues have access to opportunities based on their skills, experience, and contributions. Our hiring practices emphasise fairness, transparency, and merit, ensuring that we attract and retain the best talent. By valuing different perspectives and promoting a culture of respect and collaboration, we drive and operate the infrastructure that the world\u2019s post-trade financial system runs on","ClientSiteName":"Client Careers Site","ClientSiteXRefCode":"CANDIDATEPORTAL","CompanyName":"OSTTRA","ParentCompanyName":"OSTTRA","JobDetailsUrl":"https:\/\/jobs.dayforcehcm.com\/en-US\/osttrahcm\/CANDIDATEPORTAL\/jobs\/904","ApplyUrl":"https:\/\/jobs.dayforcehcm.com\/en-US\/osttrahcm\/CANDIDATEPORTAL\/jobs\/904\/apply","City":"Stockholm","State":"Stockholm County","Country":"SE","PostalCode":"","JobFamily":"Technology","DatePosted":"2026-07-08T00:00:00","LastUpdated":"2026-07-08T13:37:05.513","ReferenceNumber":904,"CultureCode":"en-US","ParentRequisitionCode":176,"MinHiringRate":63000,"MaxHiringRate":68000,"JobType":0,"TravelRequired":0,"IsVirtualLocation":false},{"Title":"Client Services- Operations Analyst","Description":"Job Overview\n\n\nAbout the Role:\nThe team:\nThe Client Service and Onboarding team assist clients with new client set ups and UAT testing prior to go-live in the Production environment and the team is also responsible to assist existing clients with daily queries pertaining to Production environment. Together, the FX & Security Client Service department functions within a fast-paced environment with a strong client orientation.\n\nResponsibilities and impact:\n   \u2022 Assist on everyday client queries pertaining to access management, system workflow, technical errors, and customization requirements.\n   \u2022 Manage a high level of direct client interaction via emails and phone hotlines.\n   \u2022 Act as the primary point person for incident management for Osttra-wide incidents impacting our globally based clients during APAC hours.\n   \u2022 Provide Major Incident reporting following any Severity 1 outages per SLA and monitor client query queues to resolve exceptions.\n   \u2022 Participate in internal testing of applications prior to any change going live in production and work closely with internal teams for system enhancements.\n   \u2022 Communicate and assist internal departments for onboarding new participants in a timely manner and roll out new products.\nWhat we\u2019re looking for:\nFundamental requirement:\nWe are looking for self-driven, client focused individuals with great problem solving and analytical skills to fill an Associate position within the Operations group. The successful candidate must be fluent in both English and Japanese to support our global and regional client base, and will be responsible for providing day-to-day customer support for all services supported within Osttra\u2019s suite of products.\n\n  Additional preferred requirements:\n   \u2022 University graduates preferred with work experience in the financial markets, preferably in operations.\n   \u2022 Knowledge of OTC \/ FX \/ Equity \/ Future products, the trade clearing process, and application support.\n   \u2022 Excellent interpersonal, written, and verbal communication skills in English and Japanese.\n   \u2022 Strong customer service, problem-solving skills, and a strong focus on Operational Control and Data Security.\nThe location: Tokyo -Japan\n\n\nOur Benefits: Global vision, local impact\n\n   \u2022 At OSTTRA, our benefits philosophy offers a market-competitive package that reflects our position as an industry leader. We want to ensure you feel valued, secure, and empowered wherever you are in the world.\n   \u2022 Our approach is built on three core pillars:\n   \u2022 Global foundations: We provide a baseline of excellence across all our offices, focusing on comprehensive Health & Wellness, Financial Security, and Work-Life Balance. No matter your location, you are part of a culture that prioritizes your holistic well-being.\n\n   \u2022 Locally tailored: We benchmark in each market to ensure our packages are genuinely competitive where you live and work.\n\n   \u2022 Flexibility and growth: We empower you to work in a way that suits your life. This includes a hybrid working model, generous leave policies, and a commitment to your continuous professional development.\n\nThe Trust employee ownership plan\n\nEvery employee at OSTTRA is an owner, and a member of The Trust, our employee ownership programme. Our distinct culture encourages colleagues to think and act like owners and raise the bar constantly. This plan reflects our belief that when we work together to build a stronger, more valuable organisation, then all colleagues should benefit from the value we create.\n\nAbout OSTTRA\n\nWe build and operate the infrastructure that the world\u2019s post-trade financial system runs on. Launched in 2021, we have unified more than 20 years of heritage and expertise from four industry leaders into a single, integrated business.\n\nToday,we operate a trusted network that connects thousands of market participants to streamline end-to-end workflows, from trade capture through portfolio optimisation.We translate industry change into workable process, engineering an open, intelligent ecosystem that removes friction and reduces risk for the global markets.\n\nOur distinct ownership culture is underpinned by four behaviours: boldness, curiosity, accountability, and collaboration. In 2025 we were acquired by KKR, one of the world\u2019s most successful private equity firms, and are on a journey of growth and impact.\n\nJoining our team now is a unique opportunity - you will help to shape the next generation of post-trade, transform shared infrastructure into shared benefit, and accelerate your own career. Learn more atwww.osttra.com.\n\nEqual opportunity employer statement at OSTTRA\n\nWe are committed to fostering a connected and engaged workplace where all colleagues have access to opportunities based on their skills, experience, and contributions. Our hiring practices emphasise fairness, transparency, and merit, ensuring that we attract and retain the best talent. By valuing different perspectives and promoting a culture of respect and collaboration, we drive and operate the infrastructure that the world\u2019s post-trade financial system runs on","ClientSiteName":"Client Careers Site","ClientSiteXRefCode":"CANDIDATEPORTAL","CompanyName":"OSTTRA","ParentCompanyName":"OSTTRA","JobDetailsUrl":"https:\/\/jobs.dayforcehcm.com\/en-US\/osttrahcm\/CANDIDATEPORTAL\/jobs\/930","ApplyUrl":"https:\/\/jobs.dayforcehcm.com\/en-US\/osttrahcm\/CANDIDATEPORTAL\/jobs\/930\/apply","City":"","State":"Tokyo","Country":"JP","PostalCode":"","JobFamily":"Client Services","EmploymentIndicator":"Regular","DatePosted":"2026-07-08T20:30:00","LastUpdated":"2026-07-09T12:58:01.04","ReferenceNumber":930,"CultureCode":"en-US","ParentRequisitionCode":163,"JobType":0,"TravelRequired":0,"IsVirtualLocation":false},{"Title":"Client Services-Operations Analyst ","Description":"About the Role:\nThe team:\nThe Client Service and Onboarding team assist clients with new client set ups and UAT testing prior to go-live in the Production environment and the team is also responsible to assist existing clients with daily queries pertaining to Production environment. Together, the FX & Security Client Service department functions within a fast-paced environment with a strong client orientation.\n\nResponsibilities and impact:\n   \u2022 Assist on everyday client queries pertaining to access management, system workflow, technical errors, and customization requirements.\n   \u2022 Manage a high level of direct client interaction via emails and phone hotlines.\n   \u2022 Act as the primary point person for incident management for Osttra-wide incidents impacting our globally based clients during APAC hours.\n   \u2022 Provide Major Incident reporting following any Severity 1 outages per SLA and monitor client query queues to resolve exceptions.\n   \u2022 Participate in internal testing of applications prior to any change going live in production and work closely with internal teams for system enhancements.\n   \u2022 Communicate and assist internal departments for onboarding new participants in a timely manner and roll out new products.\nWhat we\u2019re looking for:\nFundamental requirement:\nWe are looking for self-driven, client focused individuals with great problem solving and analytical skills to fill an Associate position within the Operations group. The successful candidate must be fluent in both English and Japanese to support our global and regional client base, and will be responsible for providing day-to-day customer support for all services supported within Osttra\u2019s suite of products.\n\n  Additional preferred requirements:\n   \u2022 University graduates preferred with work experience in the financial markets, preferably in operations.\n   \u2022 Knowledge of OTC \/ FX \/ Equity \/ Future products, the trade clearing process, and application support.\n   \u2022 Excellent interpersonal, written, and verbal communication skills in English and Japanese.\n   \u2022 Strong customer service, problem-solving skills, and a strong focus on Operational Control and Data Security.\nThe location: Tokyo -Japan","ClientSiteName":"Client Careers Site","ClientSiteXRefCode":"CANDIDATEPORTAL","CompanyName":"OSTTRA","ParentCompanyName":"OSTTRA","JobDetailsUrl":"https:\/\/jobs.dayforcehcm.com\/en-SG\/osttrahcm\/CANDIDATEPORTAL\/jobs\/930","ApplyUrl":"https:\/\/jobs.dayforcehcm.com\/en-SG\/osttrahcm\/CANDIDATEPORTAL\/jobs\/930\/apply","City":"","State":"Tokyo","Country":"JP","PostalCode":"","JobFamily":"Client Services","EmploymentIndicator":"Regular","DatePosted":"2026-07-08T20:30:00","LastUpdated":"2026-07-09T12:58:01.04","ReferenceNumber":930,"CultureCode":"en-SG","ParentRequisitionCode":163,"JobType":0,"TravelRequired":0,"IsVirtualLocation":false},{"Title":"Dayforce Administrator","Description":"Job Overview\n\n\nAbout the Role:\nThe team:\nThis role will be part of a newly formed team within Corporate Technology whose role is to support Finance and HR. They will be responsible for all of the technology services that are provided internally and by vendors.\nResponsibilities and impact:\nThe Dayforce Administrator and Technical Lead will manage OSTTRA\u2019s HCM platform, overseeing the end-to-end lifecycle, configuration, and maintenance of the Dayforce system in Gurugram. This leadership role requires deep technical expertise to drive automation, secure system architecture, and manage complex integrations while executing strategic technical roadmaps.\n\u25cf  Platform Operations: Lead the end-to-end operational lifecycle, including advanced configuration, maintenance, and support to ensure optimal Dayforce platform performance.\n\u25cf  Release & Change Management: Manage the deployment of system updates, patches, and feature releases in strict compliance with internal Change Advisory Board (CAB) protocols.\n\u25cf  Environment Stability: Maintain the health and data privacy of non-production environments (staging and testing) to ensure zero disruption to live business and payroll operations.\n\u25cf  Integration Oversight: Monitor and optimize technical connectors, background jobs, and APIs to ensure seamless, error-free data flows between Dayforce, SAP ERP, and other corporate tools.\n\u25cf  Security & Audit Readiness: Implement technical configurations for automated controls, segregation of duties (SoD), and user profile validation to ensure readiness for security audits.\n\u25cf  Data Governance & Compliance: Act as the primary gatekeeper for database health, ensuring the platform complies with global privacy frameworks (e.g., GDPR) and internal financial regulations.\n\u25cf  Leadership & Collaboration: Partner with external vendors and cross-functional technology and business teams to manage project delivery and translate technical roadmaps into stable solutions.\n\n  What we\u2019re looking for:\n\u25cf  Platform Mastery: Demonstrable expertise in managing the Dayforce HCM ecosystem, specifically across Core HR, Payroll, and Learning modules.\n\u25cf  Security Architecture: Advanced capability in configuring robust security architectures, including automated controls, role permissions, and session isolation parameters to ensure strict compliance.\n\u25cf  Technical Integration: Strong understanding of enterprise technology architecture, including data schemas, middleware, and integration methods required for seamless system connectivity.\n\u25cf  Vendor Management: Proven ability to manage professional services and SaaS vendor relationships, holding external partners strictly accountable to established technical SLAs.\n\u25cf  Operational Execution: A consistent track record of translating technology strategies into stable, compliant operational plans while maintaining full ownership of platform performance.\n\u25cf  Stakeholder Communication: Ability to bridge the gap between technical development teams and corporate stakeholders (Finance, HR) by clearly articulating complex technical issues and progress.\nWhat Success Looks Like (12\u201318 Months)\n\u25cf   Platform Stabilization (6 Months): Achieve and maintain a high user satisfaction score regarding the stability, security, and profile isolation configurations of the Dayforce platform post-separation.\n\u25cf   System Optimization & Efficiency (12 Months): Partner with HR to deliver technical automation projects that measurably optimize core business processes, reducing manual data intervention and increasing operational velocity.\n\u25cf  Operational Excellence (Ongoing): Deliver all ongoing platform changes, security updates, and routine maintenance with a low disruption rate to critical financial close and payroll processing operations.\n\n The location: Gurgaon, India\nOur Benefits: Global vision, local impact\nAt OSTTRA, our benefits philosophy offers a market-competitive package that reflects our position as an industry leader. We want to ensure you feel valued, secure, and empowered wherever you are in the world.\nOur approach is built on three core pillars:\n   \u2022 Global foundations: We provide a baseline of excellence across all our offices, focusing on comprehensive Health & Wellness, Financial Security, and Work-Life Balance. No matter your location, you are part of a culture that prioritizes your holistic well-being.\n   \u2022 Locally tailored: We benchmark in each market to ensure our packages are genuinely competitive where you live and work.\n   \u2022 Flexibility and growth: We empower you to work in a way that suits your life. This includes a hybrid working model, generous leave policies, and a commitment to your continuous professional development.\n\nThe Trust employee ownership plan\nEvery employee at OSTTRA is an owner, and a member of The Trust, our employee ownership programme. Our distinct culture encourages colleagues to think and act like owners and raise the bar constantly. This plan reflects our belief that when we work together to build a stronger, more valuable organisation, then all colleagues should benefit from the value we create.\nAbout OSTTRA\nWe build and operate the infrastructure that the world\u2019s post-trade financial system runs on. Launched in 2021, we have unified more than 20 years of heritage and expertise from four industry leaders into a single, integrated business.\n Today,we operate a trusted network that connects thousands of market participants to streamline end-to-end workflows, from trade capture through portfolio optimisation.We translate industry change into workable process, engineering an open, intelligent ecosystem that removes friction and reduces risk for the global markets.\nOur distinct ownership culture is underpinned by four behaviours: boldness, curiosity, accountability, and collaboration. In 2025 we were acquired by KKR, one of the world\u2019s most successful private equity firms, and are on a journey of growth and impact.\nJoining our team now is a unique opportunity - you will help to shape the next generation of post-trade, transform shared infrastructure into shared benefit, and accelerate your own career. Learn more atwww.osttra.com.\nEqual opportunity employer statement at OSTTRA\nWe are committed to fostering a connected and engaged workplace where all colleagues have access to opportunities based on their skills, experience, and contributions. Our hiring practices emphasise fairness, transparency, and merit, ensuring that we attract and retain the best talent. By valuing different perspectives and promoting a culture of respect and collaboration, we drive and operate the infrastructure that the world\u2019s post-trade financial system runs on","ClientSiteName":"Client Careers Site","ClientSiteXRefCode":"CANDIDATEPORTAL","CompanyName":"OSTTRA","ParentCompanyName":"OSTTRA","JobDetailsUrl":"https:\/\/jobs.dayforcehcm.com\/en-US\/osttrahcm\/CANDIDATEPORTAL\/jobs\/950","ApplyUrl":"https:\/\/jobs.dayforcehcm.com\/en-US\/osttrahcm\/CANDIDATEPORTAL\/jobs\/950\/apply","City":"Gurugram","State":"HR","Country":"IN","PostalCode":"","JobFamily":"Technology","DatePosted":"2026-07-11T20:30:00","LastUpdated":"2026-07-30T12:35:03.083","ReferenceNumber":950,"CultureCode":"en-US","ParentRequisitionCode":215,"JobType":0,"TravelRequired":0,"IsVirtualLocation":false},{"Title":"Sr. Application Support Engineer","Description":"Job Overview\n\n\nThe Role: Sr. Application Support Engineer\nThe Team: Application Support is a global team that provides technical support across the suite of OSTTRA products. The application support team works closely with a highly competent Client Services team and the core project teams to resolve client issues whilst continually improving our platforms. Our work helps ensure that OSTTRA provides a high-quality service and maintains client satisfaction.\nThe Impact: Together, we build, support, protect and manage high-performance, resilient platforms that process more than 100 million messages a day. Our services are vital to automated trade processing around the globe, managing peak volumes and working with our customers and regulators to ensure the efficient settlement of trades and effective operation of global capital markets.\nWhat\u2019s in it for you:\nOSTTRA is seeking an Application Support professional to join the Application Support Team. The role encompasses 2nd line technical application support as well as integration support for our Trade Processing applications. This person will report directly to the regional support manager and work closely with an experienced global team to contribute to the quality of our support.\nYou will have 10-15 years\u2019 experience of Sr. Application Support & Project Management to meet the needs of our expanding portfolio of Financial Services clients.\nThis role presents an excellent opportunity to be part of an agile team based out of Japan, collaborating with colleagues across multiple regions globally, with a strong focus on delivering value through self-service.\n Responsibilities:\n   \u2022 Your duties will include providing technical L2 and L3 support to both internal and external customers across our full suite of OTC Derivative products and FX for post-trade confirmation processing.\n   \u2022 You will need to demonstrate excellent communication skills and have a natural ability to learn with a keen interest in technology. You must be a team player and enjoy working in a high-performance collaborative global group.\n   \u2022 The successful candidate will need to be able to apply strong technical skills and good business knowledge, together with investigative techniques and problem-solving skills to identify and resolve issues in a timely and high-quality manner.\n   \u2022 Liaising with other team members, Product, Development and particularly the infrastructure teams as required for 3rd line escalation. Technical advisory will be required at times by Product and business or clients for solution delivery.\n   \u2022 Working directly with clients, to understand and resolve issues and liaising with delivery teams to ensure readiness for new platform releases. Based in our Gurgaon office, you will be responsible for handling escalations, identifying and communicating technical resolutions in English.\n   \u2022 You will also work on initiatives around platform industrialization, proactive application health monitoring and reporting.\n\nWhat We\u2019re Looking For:\n   \u2022 University graduate or equivalent with background of bachelor\u2019s in computer science.\n   \u2022 Ability to read and trace Java, C++ and\/or scripting languages.\n   \u2022 Possess the understanding of PAAS and implementation with OpenShift.\n   \u2022 Experience or having high motivation to pick up cloud implementation on AWS.\n   \u2022 Experience in handling client issues and expectation management.\n   \u2022 Experience in Application Support, software development and deployment (SDLC).\n   \u2022 Good Unix skills, including scripting experience.\n   \u2022 Experience of XML and XSLT.\n   \u2022 Experience of databases including SQL scripting, preferably but not limited to Oracle.\n   \u2022 Good understanding of messaging platforms and protocols like FIX and IBM MQ.\n   \u2022 Understanding of networking principles, its practical uses and basic troubleshooting.\n   \u2022 Experience in encrypted connectivity channels utilizing SSL and TLS.\n   \u2022 Have experience of working in the Finance Industry.\n   \u2022 Knowledge of the Financial OTC Derivative and FX products.\n   \u2022 Good understanding of Application Support processes.\n   \u2022 Awareness of Derivatives products and post trade processing (desirable).\n   \u2022 Be flexible regarding hours including weekends and public holidays.\n   \u2022 Knowledge of financial protocols like FIX, FPmL, TOF etc\n   \u2022 Ability to understand Application architecture, and able to effectively navigate to the problem area.\n   \u2022 Ability to apply analytic methodology, such as trending, distribution etc., to get insight from application data to help troubleshooting.\n   \u2022 Ability to understand business workflow and tie to technical implementation.\n\nThe location: Gurgaon,India\nOur Benefits: Global vision, local impact\nAt OSTTRA, our benefits philosophy offers a market-competitive package that reflects our position as an industry leader. We want to ensure you feel valued, secure, and empowered wherever you are in the world.\nOur approach is built on three core pillars:\n   \u2022 Global foundations: We provide a baseline of excellence across all our offices, focusing on comprehensive Health & Wellness, Financial Security, and Work-Life Balance. No matter your location, you are part of a culture that prioritizes your holistic well-being.\n   \u2022 Locally tailored: We benchmark in each market to ensure our packages are genuinely competitive where you live and work.\n   \u2022 Flexibility and growth: We empower you to work in a way that suits your life. This includes a hybrid working model, generous leave policies, and a commitment to your continuous professional development.\n\nThe Trust employee ownership plan\nEvery employee at OSTTRA is an owner, and a member of The Trust, our employee ownership programme. Our distinct culture encourages colleagues to think and act like owners and raise the bar constantly. This plan reflects our belief that when we work together to build a stronger, more valuable organisation, then all colleagues should benefit from the value we create.\nAbout OSTTRA\nWe build and operate the infrastructure that the world\u2019s post-trade financial system runs on. Launched in 2021, we have unified more than 20 years of heritage and expertise from four industry leaders into a single, integrated business.\nToday,we operate a trusted network that connects thousands of market participants to streamline end-to-end workflows, from trade capture through portfolio optimisation.We translate industry change into workable process, engineering an open, intelligent ecosystem that removes friction and reduces risk for the global markets.\nOur distinct ownership culture is underpinned by four behaviours: boldness, curiosity, accountability, and collaboration. In 2025 we were acquired by KKR, one of the world\u2019s most successful private equity firms, and are on a journey of growth and impact.\nJoining our team now is a unique opportunity - you will help to shape the next generation of post-trade, transform shared infrastructure into shared benefit, and accelerate your own career. Learn more atwww.osttra.com.\nEqual opportunity employer statement at OSTTRA\nWe are committed to fostering a connected and engaged workplace where all colleagues have access to opportunities based on their skills, experience, and contributions. Our hiring practices emphasise fairness, transparency, and merit, ensuring that we attract and retain the best talent. By valuing different perspectives and promoting a culture of respect and collaboration, we drive and operate the infrastructure that the world\u2019s post-trade financial system runs on\n\n\nOur Benefits: Global vision, local impact\n\nAt OSTTRA, our benefits philosophy offers a market-competitive package that reflects our position as an industry leader. We want to ensure you feel valued, secure, and empowered wherever you are in the world.\nOur approach is built on three core pillars:\n\n   \u2022 Global foundations: We provide a baseline of excellence across all our offices, focusing on comprehensive Health & Wellness, Financial Security, and Work-Life Balance. No matter your location, you are part of a culture that prioritizes your holistic well-being.\n   \u2022 Locally tailored: We benchmark in each market to ensure our packages are genuinely competitive where you live and work.\n   \u2022 Flexibility and growth: We empower you to work in a way that suits your life. This includes a hybrid working model, generous leave policies, and a commitment to your continuous professional development.\n\nThe Trust employee ownership plan\n Every employee at OSTTRA is an owner, and a member of The Trust, our employee ownership programme. Our distinct culture encourages colleagues to think and act like owners and raise the bar constantly. This plan reflects our belief that when we work together to build a stronger, more valuable organisation, then all colleagues should benefit from the value we create.\n\nAbout OSTTRA\nWe build and operate the infrastructure that the world\u2019s post-trade financial system runs on. Launched in 2021, we have unified more than 20 years of heritage and expertise from four industry leaders into a single, integrated business.\nToday, we operate a trusted network that connects thousands of market participants to streamline end-to-end workflows, from trade capture through portfolio optimization. We translate industry change into a workable process, engineering an open, intelligent ecosystem that removes friction and reduces risk for the global markets.\nOur distinct ownership culture is underpinned by four behaviours: boldness, curiosity, accountability, and collaboration. In 2025 we were acquired by KKR, one of the world\u2019s most successful private equity firms, and are on a journey of growth and impact.\nJoining our team now is a unique opportunity - you will help to shape the next generation of post-trade, transform shared infrastructure into shared benefit, and accelerate your own career. Learn more atwww.osttra.com.\nEqual opportunity employer statement at OSTTRA\nWe are committed to fostering a connected and engaged workplace where all colleagues have access to opportunities based on their skills, experience, and contributions. Our hiring practices emphasise fairness, transparency, and merit, ensuring that we attract and retain the best talent. By valuing different perspectives and promoting a culture of respect and collaboration, we drive and operate the infrastructure that the world\u2019s post-trade financial system runs on","ClientSiteName":"Client Careers Site","ClientSiteXRefCode":"CANDIDATEPORTAL","CompanyName":"OSTTRA","ParentCompanyName":"OSTTRA","JobDetailsUrl":"https:\/\/jobs.dayforcehcm.com\/en-US\/osttrahcm\/CANDIDATEPORTAL\/jobs\/1007","ApplyUrl":"https:\/\/jobs.dayforcehcm.com\/en-US\/osttrahcm\/CANDIDATEPORTAL\/jobs\/1007\/apply","City":"","State":"Tokyo","Country":"JP","PostalCode":"","JobFamily":"Technology","DatePosted":"2026-07-26T20:30:00","LastUpdated":"2026-07-30T12:22:53.093","ReferenceNumber":1007,"CultureCode":"en-US","ParentRequisitionCode":233,"JobType":0,"TravelRequired":0,"IsVirtualLocation":false},{"Title":"Senior Client Services Associate (Trade Processing) ","Description":"Job Overview\n\n\nAbout the Role:\nThe team:\nThe Trade Processing Client Services team is the first line of contact for our clients to provide day-to-day operational client support of OSTTRA platforms that provide trade capture, trade processing, give up messaging, and credit management workflows.\nYou will provide essential client support while collaborating closely with Commercial, Product, Technology, Sales, and Customer Success teams across the globe.\n\nResponsibilities and impact:\nYou will be supporting a diverse and high-profile client base, including leading banks, hedge funds, asset managers, and fund administrators. Our services are deeply embedded in their systems.\nIn this role, you will be instrumental in providing effective support to our clients through the following duties and responsibilities\n   \u2022 Build trusted client relationships as the face of the global Client Services team through online engagements and face-to-face meetings.\n\n   \u2022 Act as an escalation point or a single point of contact for initiatives, services or projects from a Client Services perspective.\n\n   \u2022 Communicate incident status to clients, client enhancement requests to internal Product and Technology teams;\n\n   \u2022 Coordinate across the global Client Services team to ensure consistent, positive client outcomes.\n\n   \u2022 Participate in various initiatives and projects through testing system enhancements, identifying and tracking issues, and collaborate across Product and Technology teams for successful delivery.\n\n   \u2022 Manage and resolve operational queries related to access management, trade message workflows, configuration change requests, and errors and exceptions. You will partner closely with internal teams to ensure prompt and complete resolution.\n\n   \u2022 Conduct testing and troubleshooting; escalating complex and critical issues to Technology for deep-dive analysis.\n\n   \u2022 Deliver productive training and demonstrations to both new clients and team members, in person or through online communication tools.\n\n   \u2022 Provide onboarding and user acceptance testing support by configuring platforms for key trade capture and messaging workflows, and user access.\nWhat we\u2019re looking for:\nFundamental requirement:\n   \u2022 Communication: You must have strong communication skills\u2014you write, speak, and present clearly and effectively, with the ability to build and maintain client relationships and to work cross-functionally.\n\n   \u2022 Problem-Solving: You are a good listener, think critically, and can analyse information to solve problems. You have the ability to analyse data to identify trends and areas of improvement.\n\n   \u2022 Client Focus: You are dedicated to providing a positive client experience and understand the impact of your actions on both internal and external partners.You understand and prioritize client confidentiality and data security.\n\n   \u2022 Organisational Agility: You can independently handle multiple tasks, manage priorities, and thrive in a fast-paced environment.\n Additional preferred requirements:\n   \u2022 Tech Literacy: You are comfortable using basic software tools, including text editors and spreadsheet functions. Advanced spreadsheet skills or familiarity with the basics of how software is built (Software Development Lifecycle concepts) is preferred.\n\n   \u2022 English Fluency: Fluency in English is essential. Proficiency in another language is a plus.\n\n   \u2022 Industry Experience: Prior experience in the Financial Services industry and\/or familiarity with financial markets, OTC derivatives, credit management, or post-trade processing is preferred.\n\n   \u2022 Cultivating Collaboration: You have the ability to foster a highly collaborative team culture through knowledge sharing, mentoring team members, and navigating interactions with other departments and key stakeholders.\n\nThe location: London, United Kingdom\nRight to work requirements:\nThis role is limited to persons with indefinite right to work in the UK.\nOur Benefits: Global vision, local impact\nAt OSTTRA, our benefits philosophy offers a market-competitive package that reflects our position as an industry leader. We want to ensure you feel valued, secure, and empowered wherever you are in the world.\nOur approach is built on three core pillars:\n   \u2022 Global foundations: We provide a baseline of excellence across all our offices, focusing on comprehensive Health & Wellness, Financial Security, and Work-Life Balance. No matter your location, you are part of a culture that prioritizes your holistic well-being.\n   \u2022 Locally tailored: We benchmark in each market to ensure our packages are genuinely competitive where you live and work.\n   \u2022 Flexibility and growth: We empower you to work in a way that suits your life. This includes a hybrid working model, generous leave policies, and a commitment to your continuous professional development.\n\nThe Trust employee ownership plan\nEvery employee at OSTTRA is an owner, and a member of The Trust, our employee ownership programme. Our distinct culture encourages colleagues to think and act like owners and raise the bar constantly.\nThis plan reflects our belief that when we work together to build a stronger, more valuable organisation, then all colleagues should benefit from the value we create.\nAbout OSTTRA\nWe build and operate the infrastructure that the world\u2019s post-trade financial system runs on. Launched in 2021, we have unified more than 20 years of heritage and expertise from four industry leaders into a single, integrated business.\nToday,we operate a trusted network that connects thousands of market participants to streamline end-to-end workflows, from trade capture through portfolio optimisation.We translate industry change into workable process, engineering an open, intelligent ecosystem that removes friction and reduces risk for the global markets.\n\nOur distinct ownership culture is underpinned by four behaviours: boldness, curiosity, accountability, and collaboration. In 2025 we were acquired by KKR, one of the world\u2019s most successful private equity firms, and are on a journey of growth and impact.\nJoining our team now is a unique opportunity - you will help to shape the next generation of post-trade, transform shared infrastructure into shared benefit, and accelerate your own career. Learn more at www.osttra.com.\nEqual opportunity employer statement at OSTTRA:\nWe are committed to fostering a connected and engaged workplace where all colleagues have access to opportunities based on their skills, experience, and contributions. Our hiring practices emphasise fairness, transparency, and merit, ensuring that we attract and retain the best talent. By valuing different perspectives and promoting a culture of respect and collaboration, we drive and operate the infrastructure that the world\u2019s post-trade financial system runs on.","ClientSiteName":"Client Careers Site","ClientSiteXRefCode":"CANDIDATEPORTAL","CompanyName":"OSTTRA","ParentCompanyName":"OSTTRA","JobDetailsUrl":"https:\/\/jobs.dayforcehcm.com\/en-US\/osttrahcm\/CANDIDATEPORTAL\/jobs\/1088","ApplyUrl":"https:\/\/jobs.dayforcehcm.com\/en-US\/osttrahcm\/CANDIDATEPORTAL\/jobs\/1088\/apply","City":"London","State":"England","Country":"GB","PostalCode":"","JobFamily":"Client Services","DatePosted":"2026-08-03T00:00:00","LastUpdated":"2026-08-03T13:52:17.83","ReferenceNumber":1088,"CultureCode":"en-US","ParentRequisitionCode":179,"JobType":0,"TravelRequired":0,"IsVirtualLocation":false},{"Title":"Sr Ops Analysis Analyst (Korean\/Japanese speaking)","Description":"Job Overview\n\n\nAbout the Role:\nThe team:\nWe are looking for self-driven, client focused individuals with great problem solving and analytical skills to fill an Associate position within the Operations group.  The successful candidate will be responsible for providing day-to-day customer support for all services supported within Osttra\u2019s suite of products.\nThe Onboarding team assists clients with new client set ups and UAT testing prior to go-live in the Production environment. Client Services team is responsible to assist existing clients with daily queries pertaining to the Production environment.\nResponsibilities and impact:\n   \u2022 As part of platform \/ system support, individuals are required to assist on everyday client queries pertaining to access management, system workflow, technical errors, customization requirements etc.\n   \u2022 High level of direct client interaction. Client queries handled via emails and phone hotline.\n   \u2022 Act as the primary point person for incident management for Osttra-wide incident impacting our globally based clients during APAC hours. Incident management responsibilities include:\n   \u2022 Response to initial incident notification\n   \u2022 Providing regular updates to clients per SLA\n   \u2022 Primary liaison for aiding our clients through post-incident recovery\n   \u2022 Provide Major Incident reporting following any Severity 1 outages per SLA.\n   \u2022 Participate in internal testing of applications, prior to any change going live in production.\n   \u2022 Work closely with internal teams for system enhancements.\n   \u2022 Ensuring accurate input of static data client profile configurations are processed daily and the team meets assigned targets and SLA\u2019s.\n   \u2022 Monitor client query queues, diagnose and resolve any resulting exceptions or errors and work with internal groups to provide resolution.\n   \u2022 Respond to client requests by providing detailed analysis and feedback.\n   \u2022 Process reports (user list \/ Trade) as requested by clients.\n   \u2022 Participate in internal \/ external training needs. Educate clients on upcoming changes.\n   \u2022 Liaise with participants for rolling out new products\n   \u2022 Communicate and assist internal departments for onboarding new participants in a timely manner and effective implementation of the product.\nWhat we\u2019re looking for:\nBusiness competencies\nEducation and experience\n   \u2022 University graduate preferred\n   \u2022 Work experience in the financial markets preferably in operations\n   \u2022 Knowledge of OTC \/ FX\/Equity\/Future products, the trade clearing process and application support a major plus\n   \u2022 Prior experience working on Traiana\/MarkitServ applications is a major plus\n   \u2022 Business level proficiency for Korean\/Japanese is preferred\nCommercial awareness\n   \u2022  Ability to work in fast paced environment with client orientation\nManagement requirements\n   \u2022   Not applicable\nPersonal competencies\nPersonal impact\n   \u2022 Strong customer service and problem-solving skills\n   \u2022 Focused on Operational Control and Data Security\n   \u2022 Flexible and able to adapt to change\n   \u2022 Able to work independently with minimal supervision\nCommunication\n   \u2022 Excellent interpersonal, written and verbal communication skills\nTeamwork\n   \u2022 Customer service and satisfaction are key priorities for the firm. Candidates must be aware of the impact of their actions on internal and external clients\nThe location: Penang  Malaysia\nOur Benefits: Global vision, local impact\nAt OSTTRA, our benefits philosophy offers a market-competitive package that reflects our position as an industry leader. We want to ensure you feel valued, secure, and empowered wherever you are in the world.\nOur approach is built on three core pillars:\n   \u2022 Global foundations: We provide a baseline of excellence across all our offices, focusing on comprehensive Health & Wellness, Financial Security, and Work-Life Balance. No matter your location, you are part of a culture that prioritizes your holistic well-being.\n   \u2022 Locally tailored: We benchmark in each market to ensure our packages are genuinely competitive where you live and work.\n   \u2022 Flexibility and growth: We empower you to work in a way that suits your life. This includes a hybrid working model, generous leave policies, and a commitment to your continuous professional development.\n\nThe Trust employee ownership plan\nEvery employee at OSTTRA is an owner, and a member of The Trust, our employee ownership programme. Our distinct culture encourages colleagues to think and act like owners and raise the bar constantly.\nThis plan reflects our belief that when we work together to build a stronger, more valuable organisation, then all colleagues should benefit from the value we create.About OSTTRA\nWe build and operate the infrastructure that the world\u2019s post-trade financial system runs on. Launched in 2021, we have unified more than 20 years of heritage and expertise from four industry leaders into a single, integrated business.\nToday,we operate a trusted network that connects thousands of market participants to streamline end-to-end workflows, from trade capture through portfolio optimisation.We translate industry change into workable process, engineering an open, intelligent ecosystem that removes friction and reduces risk for the global markets.\n\nOur distinct ownership culture is underpinned by four behaviours: boldness, curiosity, accountability, and collaboration. In 2025 we were acquired by KKR, one of the world\u2019s most successful private equity firms, and are on a journey of growth and impact.\nJoining our team now is a unique opportunity - you will help to shape the next generation of post-trade, transform shared infrastructure into shared benefit, and accelerate your own career. Learn more at www.osttra.com.\nEqual opportunity employer statement at OSTTRA:\nWe are committed to fostering a connected and engaged workplace where all colleagues have access to opportunities based on their skills, experience, and contributions. Our hiring practices emphasise fairness, transparency, and merit, ensuring that we attract and retain the best talent. By valuing different perspectives and promoting a culture of respect and collaboration, we drive and operate the infrastructure that the world\u2019s post-trade financial system runs on.","ClientSiteName":"Client Careers Site","ClientSiteXRefCode":"CANDIDATEPORTAL","CompanyName":"OSTTRA","ParentCompanyName":"OSTTRA","JobDetailsUrl":"https:\/\/jobs.dayforcehcm.com\/en-US\/osttrahcm\/CANDIDATEPORTAL\/jobs\/1113","ApplyUrl":"https:\/\/jobs.dayforcehcm.com\/en-US\/osttrahcm\/CANDIDATEPORTAL\/jobs\/1113\/apply","City":"","State":"Penang","Country":"MY","PostalCode":"","JobFamily":"Client Services","DatePosted":"2026-08-10T20:30:00","LastUpdated":"2026-08-12T09:22:44.77","ReferenceNumber":1113,"CultureCode":"en-US","ParentRequisitionCode":214,"JobType":0,"TravelRequired":0,"IsVirtualLocation":false},{"Title":"Sr. Information Security Engineer (GRC)","Description":"Job Overview\n\n\nAbout the Role:\nThe team:\nThe Information Security team is responsible for security controls relating to protecting information in all formats. We maintain a number of policies and an Information Security Management System which dictates how infosec is integrated into processes as well as tools and technical controls to directly protect against cyber security threats.\nResponsibilities and impact:\nWe are seeking a dedicated and collaborative Sr. Information Security Engineer to join our growing Governance, Risk, and Compliance (GRC) team. In this role, you will play a pivotal part in maintaining, maturing, and auditing our information security management framework.\nThe ideal candidate has 5\u20138 years of direct experience within an InfoSec GRC function and thrives in a team-oriented environment. You will be responsible for ensuring our policies remain up-to-date, driving our ISO 27001 certification lifecycle, and executing core compliance operations like user access reviews, exception management, and security awareness programs.\nKey Responsibilities\n Governance & ISO 27001 Management\n   \u2022 ISMS Governance: Manage and maintain our ISO 27001 Information Security Management System (ISMS) to ensure continuous compliance.\n   \u2022 Audit Facilitation: Lead internal security audits and act as a point of contact for external certification audits.\n   \u2022 Policy Management: Regularly review, update, and draft information security policies, standards, and procedures to align with evolving regulatory landscapes and business needs.\n GRC Operations & Risk Management\n   \u2022 Access Governance: Coordinate and oversee periodic user access reviews across critical systems.\n   \u2022 Exception Management: Evaluate, log, and monitor security policy exceptions, ensuring compensating controls are effectively implemented and tracked.\n   \u2022 Risk Culture: Administer the company-wide security awareness training program and orchestrate routine phishing simulations to strengthen our human firewall.\nCollaboration & Communication\n   \u2022 Partner closely with cross-functional teams (IT, Legal, HR, and Engineering) to embed security compliance into daily operations.\n   \u2022 Translate complex compliance requirements into actionable, easy-to-understand guidance for non-technical stakeholders.\nWhat we\u2019re looking for:\nRequired Experience & Skills\n   \u2022 Experience: 5\u20138 years of proven experience specifically within an Information Security GRC role.\n   \u2022 ISO 27001 Expertise: Hands-on experience managing an ISO 27001 ISMS, including active participation in both internal and external certification audits.\n   \u2022 Core GRC Competencies: Direct experience executing user access reviews, phishing simulations, security training, and policy exception workflows.\n   \u2022 Communication: Exceptional verbal and written communication skills, with the ability to document clear policies and present findings to various business units.\n   \u2022 Soft Skills: A strong team player with a highly collaborative mindset, excellent problem-solving abilities, and a proactive approach to security culture.\nPreferred Qualifications (Nice-to-Have)\n   \u2022 Relevant industry certifications (e.g., ISO 27001 Internal\/Lead Auditor, CISA, CRISC, Security+, or CISM).\n   \u2022 Experience with the ISO 42001 AIMS standard.\n   \u2022 Experience utilizing GRC automation platforms\/tools.\nThe location: Gurgaon,India\nOur Benefits: Global vision, local impact\nAt OSTTRA, our benefits philosophy offers a market-competitive package that reflects our position as an industry leader. We want to ensure you feel valued, secure, and empowered wherever you are in the world.\nOur approach is built on three core pillars:\n   \u2022 Global foundations: We provide a baseline of excellence across all our offices, focusing on comprehensive Health & Wellness, Financial Security, and Work-Life Balance. No matter your location, you are part of a culture that prioritizes your holistic well-being.\n   \u2022 Locally tailored: We benchmark in each market to ensure our packages are genuinely competitive where you live and work.\n   \u2022 Flexibility and growth: We empower you to work in a way that suits your life. This includes a hybrid working model, generous leave policies, and a commitment to your continuous professional development.\n\n The Trust employee ownership plan\nEvery employee at OSTTRA is an owner, and a member of The Trust, our employee ownership programme. Our distinct culture encourages colleagues to think and act like owners and raise the bar constantly. This plan reflects our belief that when we work together to build a stronger, more valuable organisation, then all colleagues should benefit from the value we create.\nAbout OSTTRA\nWe build and operate the infrastructure that the world\u2019s post-trade financial system runs on. Launched in 2021, we have unified more than 20 years of heritage and expertise from four industry leaders into a single, integrated business.\nToday,we operate a trusted network that connects thousands of market participants to streamline end-to-end workflows, from trade capture through portfolio optimisation.We translate industry change into workable process, engineering an open, intelligent ecosystem that removes friction and reduces risk for the global markets.\nOur distinct ownership culture is underpinned by four behaviours: boldness, curiosity, accountability, and collaboration. In 2025 we were acquired by KKR, one of the world\u2019s most successful private equity firms, and are on a journey of growth and impact.\nJoining our team now is a unique opportunity - you will help to shape the next generation of post-trade, transform shared infrastructure into shared benefit, and accelerate your own career. Learn more atwww.osttra.com.\nEqual opportunity employer statement at OSTTRA\nWe are committed to fostering a connected and engaged workplace where all colleagues have access to opportunities based on their skills, experience, and contributions. Our hiring practices emphasise fairness, transparency, and merit, ensuring that we attract and retain the best talent. By valuing different perspectives and promoting a culture of respect and collaboration, we drive and operate the infrastructure that the world\u2019s post-trade financial system runs on","ClientSiteName":"Client Careers Site","ClientSiteXRefCode":"CANDIDATEPORTAL","CompanyName":"OSTTRA","ParentCompanyName":"OSTTRA","JobDetailsUrl":"https:\/\/jobs.dayforcehcm.com\/en-US\/osttrahcm\/CANDIDATEPORTAL\/jobs\/1156","ApplyUrl":"https:\/\/jobs.dayforcehcm.com\/en-US\/osttrahcm\/CANDIDATEPORTAL\/jobs\/1156\/apply","City":"Gurugram","State":"HR","Country":"IN","PostalCode":"","JobFamily":"Technology","EmploymentIndicator":"Regular","DatePosted":"2026-08-24T20:30:00","LastUpdated":"2026-08-25T11:21:44.49","ReferenceNumber":1156,"CultureCode":"en-US","ParentRequisitionCode":191,"JobType":0,"TravelRequired":0,"IsVirtualLocation":false},{"Title":"Apprentice - Talent Acquisition ","Description":"Job Overview\n\n\nAbout the Role\nThe team: The Talent Acquisition team at OSTTRA is dedicated to attracting, engaging, and hiring top-tier talent to drive our global business forward. As a collaborative and fast-paced team, we partner closely with business leaders and hiring managers across regions to deliver a seamless candidate experience and strategic hiring outcomes.\nResponsibilities and impact:\n   \u2022 Assist Talent Acquisition Specialists with candidate sourcing, screening, and scheduling interviews across various departments.\n   \u2022 Maintain and update candidate records within our Applicant Tracking System (ATS), ensuring high data accuracy.\n   \u2022 Provide an exceptional candidate experience by serving as a responsive point of contact throughout the recruitment lifecycle.\n   \u2022 Help execute early-career recruitment initiatives, campus outreach, and employer branding events.\n   \u2022 Support recruiting metrics reporting and research industry trends to optimize talent acquisition processes.\n   \u2022 Gain hands-on exposure to global hiring practices, talent pipelines, and cross-functional HR operations.\nWhat we\u2019re looking for\nFundamental requirements:\n   \u2022 Bachelor\u2019s degree or equivalent foundational education in Human Resources, Business Administration, Communications, or a related field. (2025,2024 & 2023)pass out without any prior work experience can be considered for this role)\n   \u2022 Strong interest in developing a career in Talent Acquisition and Recruitment.\n   \u2022 Proficiency with standard office software (e.g., Microsoft Office Suite, Google Workspace).\n   \u2022 Excellent written and verbal communication skills.\n   \u2022 High level of empathy, active listening, and strong interpersonal skills.\n   \u2022 Detail-oriented mindset with the ability to manage time and prioritize tasks effectively.\n   \u2022 Eagerness to learn, adapt, and collaborate within a fast-moving team environment.\nAdditional preferred requirements:\n   \u2022 Prior internship or volunteer experience in HR, customer service, or administrative support.\n   \u2022 Familiarity with recruitment platforms like LinkedIn Recruiter or Applicant Tracking Systems.\n   \u2022 Proactive problem-solving abilities and a positive, team-first attitude.\nLocation- Gurgaon, India\n\nOur Benefits: Global vision, local impact\nAt OSTTRA, our benefits philosophy offers a market-competitive package that reflects our position as an industry leader. We want to ensure you feel valued, secure, and empowered wherever you are in the world.\nOur approach is built on three core pillars:\n   \u2022 Global foundations: We provide a baseline of excellence across all our offices, focusing on comprehensive Health & Wellness, Financial Security, and Work-Life Balance.\n   \u2022 Locally tailored: We benchmark in each market to ensure our packages are genuinely competitive where you live and work.\n   \u2022 Flexibility and growth: We empower you to work in a way that suits your life, including a hybrid working model, generous leave policies, and a commitment to continuous professional development.\nThe Trust employee ownership plan Every employee at OSTTRA is an owner and a member of The Trust, our employee ownership programme. Our distinct culture encourages colleagues to think and act like owners and raise the bar constantly.\nAbout OSTTRA\nWe build and operate the infrastructure that the world\u2019s post-trade financial system runs on. Launched in 2021, we have unified more than 20 years of heritage and expertise from four industry leaders into a single, integrated business.\nToday, we operate a trusted network that connects thousands of market participants to streamline end-to-end workflows, from trade capture through portfolio optimisation. We translate industry change into workable processes, engineering an open, intelligent ecosystem that removes friction and reduces risk for global markets.\nOur distinct ownership culture is underpinned by four behaviours: boldness, curiosity, accountability, and collaboration. In 2025 we were acquired by KKR, one of the world\u2019s most successful private equity firms, and are on a journey of growth and impact.\nLearn more atwww.osttra.com.\nEqual Opportunity Employer Statement\nWe are committed to fostering a connected and engaged workplace where all colleagues have access to opportunities based on their skills, experience, and contributions. Our hiring practices emphasise fairness, transparency, and merit, ensuring that we attract and retain the best talent.","ClientSiteName":"Client Careers Site","ClientSiteXRefCode":"CANDIDATEPORTAL","CompanyName":"OSTTRA","ParentCompanyName":"OSTTRA","JobDetailsUrl":"https:\/\/jobs.dayforcehcm.com\/en-US\/osttrahcm\/CANDIDATEPORTAL\/jobs\/1164","ApplyUrl":"https:\/\/jobs.dayforcehcm.com\/en-US\/osttrahcm\/CANDIDATEPORTAL\/jobs\/1164\/apply","City":"Gurugram","State":"HR","Country":"IN","PostalCode":"","JobFamily":"Human Resources","DatePosted":"2026-08-25T20:30:00","LastUpdated":"2026-08-27T10:46:58.4","ReferenceNumber":1164,"CultureCode":"en-US","ParentRequisitionCode":269,"JobType":0,"TravelRequired":0,"IsVirtualLocation":false},{"Title":"Associate II Software Engineer","Description":"Job Overview\n\n\nAbout the Role:\nThe team: Our Engineering team develops and maintains modern, cloud-based applications and AI-powered solutions that support global business operations. Team members collaborate across Product, Architecture, QA, and DevOps functions to build reliable, secure, and scalable solutions. The team embraces agile delivery practices and encourages continuous learning, innovation, and professional growth.\n\nResponsibilities and impact:\nWe are looking for a passionate and motivated Software Engineer to join our engineering team. In this role, you will be responsible for developing and delivering high-quality product features aligned with the product roadmap. You will collaborate closely with senior engineers, architects, and subject matter experts to design and implement scalable solutions that adhere to established engineering standards and reference architectures. This is an excellent opportunity to work on modern distributed systems, cloud-native technologies, AI-driven development practices, and event-driven architectures while gaining exposure to the asset management and post-trade domain.\nKey Responsibilities\n   \u2022 Product Development & Engineering Excellence: Develop, test, and deliver high-quality, scalable features while contributing to technical design, conducting code reviews, adhering to engineering best practices, and minimizing technical debt through clean coding.\n   \u2022 Agile Delivery & Collaboration: Maintain high Agile delivery standards, including effort estimation, sprint planning, and regular status updates, while collaborating with cross-functional teams to effectively translate requirements into business value.\n   \u2022 AI Integration & Development Tools: Integrate AI\/ML capabilities\u2014such as LLM-based workflows, intelligent automation, and AI-assisted decision-making\u2014into products and utilize AI-powered tools to accelerate development speed and code quality.\n   \u2022 System Architecture & Automation: Operate within distributed, service-oriented architectures while actively supporting CI\/CD initiatives and infrastructure automation, with a specific focus on AI-augmented testing and deployment strategies.\n   \u2022 Domain Expertise & Talent Acquisition: Continuously build specialized domain knowledge in asset management and post-trade processing, while contributing to organizational growth through technical interviews and hiring support.\n\nWhat we\u2019re looking for:\nRequired Skills & Qualifications\n   \u2022 Core Development Expertise: Requires a Bachelor\u2019s degree in CS\/Engineering and 3\u20135 years of hands-on development experience. Must demonstrate core proficiency in Java\/Spring Boot, React for front-end development, and SQL for database management, alongside specialized expertise in RESTful API design, AVRO\/gRPC, and event-driven architectures using Kafka.\n   \u2022 Infrastructure & Agile Environment: Demands practical experience in Agile development processes and managing CI\/CD pipelines (e.g., Jenkins, GitLab CI, GitHub Actions, Azure DevOps) within major cloud environments (AWS, Azure, or GCP).\n   \u2022 Modern Productivity & Soft Skills: Necessitates proficiency in AI-assisted development tools and prompt engineering for productivity, alongside strong analytical, troubleshooting, problem-solving, and collaboration capabilities.\n\nPreferred Skills\n   \u2022 Modern Engineering & Systems: Proficiency in modern Java (Streams, Lambda Expressions, Functional Programming) combined with experience building high-volume, distributed systems, utilizing containerization (Docker, Kubernetes), and applying stream processing technologies like Apache Spark or Apache Flink.\n   \u2022 AI Integration & Advanced Tech: Advanced capability in integrating AI APIs and LLM services (e.g., OpenAI, Azure OpenAI, LangChain) using RAG patterns, vector databases, and AI agent frameworks, alongside an understanding of Web 3.0 concepts and Distributed Ledger Technologies.\n   \u2022 Domain Expertise: Specialized domain exposure to Asset Management, Post-Trade Processing, or Reference Data platforms, facilitating the application of technical solutions within these complex financial environments.\n\nThe location: Gurgaon,India\n\nOur Benefits: Global vision, local impact\nAt OSTTRA, our benefits philosophy offers a market-competitive package that reflects our position as an industry leader. We want to ensure you feel valued, secure, and empowered wherever you are in the world.\nOur approach is built on three core pillars:\n   \u2022 Global foundations: We provide a baseline of excellence across all our offices, focusing on comprehensive Health & Wellness, Financial Security, and Work-Life Balance. No matter your location, you are part of a culture that prioritizes your holistic well-being.\n   \u2022 Locally tailored: We benchmark in each market to ensure our packages are genuinely competitive where you live and work.\n   \u2022 Flexibility and growth: We empower you to work in a way that suits your life. This includes a hybrid working model, generous leave policies, and a commitment to your continuous professional development.\n\n\nThe Trust employee ownership plan\nEvery employee at OSTTRA is an owner, and a member of The Trust, our employee ownership programme. Our distinct culture encourages colleagues to think and act like owners and raise the bar constantly. This plan reflects our belief that when we work together to build a stronger, more valuable organisation, then all colleagues should benefit from the value we create.\n\nAbout OSTTRA\nWe build and operate the infrastructure that the world\u2019s post-trade financial system runs on. Launched in 2021, we have unified more than 20 years of heritage and expertise from four industry leaders into a single, integrated business.\nToday,we operate a trusted network that connects thousands of market participants to streamline end-to-end workflows, from trade capture through portfolio optimisation.We translate industry change into workable process, engineering an open, intelligent ecosystem that removes friction and reduces risk for the global markets.\nOur distinct ownership culture is underpinned by four behaviours: boldness, curiosity, accountability, and collaboration. In 2025 we were acquired by KKR, one of the world\u2019s most successful private equity firms, and are on a journey of growth and impact.\nJoining our team now is a unique opportunity - you will help to shape the next generation of post-trade, transform shared infrastructure into shared benefit, and accelerate your own career. Learn more atwww.osttra.com.\nEqual opportunity employer statement at OSTTRA\nWe are committed to fostering a connected and engaged workplace where all colleagues have access to opportunities based on their skills, experience, and contributions. Our hiring practices emphasise fairness, transparency, and merit, ensuring that we attract and retain the best talent. By valuing different perspectives and promoting a culture of respect and collaboration, we drive and operate the infrastructure that the world\u2019s post-trade financial system runs on.","ClientSiteName":"Client Careers Site","ClientSiteXRefCode":"CANDIDATEPORTAL","CompanyName":"OSTTRA","ParentCompanyName":"OSTTRA","JobDetailsUrl":"https:\/\/jobs.dayforcehcm.com\/en-US\/osttrahcm\/CANDIDATEPORTAL\/jobs\/1174","ApplyUrl":"https:\/\/jobs.dayforcehcm.com\/en-US\/osttrahcm\/CANDIDATEPORTAL\/jobs\/1174\/apply","City":"Gurugram","State":"HR","Country":"IN","PostalCode":"","JobFamily":"Technology","DatePosted":"2026-08-26T20:30:00","LastUpdated":"2026-08-27T09:01:19.68","ReferenceNumber":1174,"CultureCode":"en-US","ParentRequisitionCode":279,"JobType":0,"TravelRequired":0,"IsVirtualLocation":false},{"Title":"Application Support Engineer","Description":"Job Overview\n\n\nAbout the Role:\nThe team:\nOSTTRA is seeking an experienced, analytical, and collaborative Application Support Engineer to join our team in New York City. In this role, you will provide critical 2nd-line technical support for our core Trade Processing applications, which are hosted across on-premises, client-premises, and cloud environments.\nReporting directly to the Regional Application Support Manager, you will work closely with a global team in a \"Follow the Sun\" model, ensuring system reliability, optimizing application health, and delivering exceptional service to our financial clients.\nResponsibilities and impact:\n   \u2022 Technical Support & Resolution: Provide 2nd-line, client-facing technical support for issues escalated by 1st-line teams. Utilize strong investigative and problem-solving skills to diagnose and resolve complex issues efficiently.\n   \u2022 Incident & System Monitoring: Proactively monitor system operations to detect anomalies. Initiate the incident management process by raising service outage tickets and driving swift resolutions.\n   \u2022 Cross-Functional Collaboration: Work closely with the Development team for 3rd-line escalations, and coordinate with Product and Delivery teams to ensure support readiness for new software releases and enhancements.\n   \u2022 Continuous Improvement: Lead initiatives focused on proactive application health monitoring, reporting automation, and operational efficiency.\n   \u2022 Global Handover: Successfully manage the seamless handover of technical issues incoming from EMEA and outgoing to APAC.\nWhat we\u2019re looking for:\nFundamental requirement:\n   \u2022 Experience: 1-2 years of experience in an Application Support, Production Support, or a similar technical role (ideally within the Financial Services industry).\n   \u2022 Education: Bachelor\u2019s degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or a related technical field (Master\u2019s degree is a plus).\n   \u2022 SDLC & JIRA: Strong understanding of the Software Development Life Cycle (SDLC) with proven experience analyzing, prioritizing, and raising development bugs in JIRA.\n   \u2022 Technical Essentials: Fundamental knowledge of SQL and RDBMS, Strong understanding of Windows and Linux operating systems, basic knowledge of networking topology and fundamentals.\n   \u2022 Process Knowledge: Solid understanding of Application Support frameworks and ITIL best practices.\n   \u2022 Flexibility: Ability to participate in occasional weekend work on a rotational basis.\n Additional preferred requirements:\n   \u2022 Scripting: Experience with scripting languages (preferably Python).\n   \u2022 Monitoring Tools: Familiarity with tools like Grafana or Centreon.\n   \u2022 Domain Expertise: Awareness of Derivatives products and Trade Processing workflows.\n   \u2022 Certifications: CCNA or ITIL certifications are a strong advantage.\nThe location: New York, United States\nRight to work requirements:\nThis role is limited to persons with indefinite right to work in the United States.\nCompensation\/benefits information:\nThe anticipated base salary range for this position is $80,000 to $90,000. Final base salary for this role will be based on the individual\u2019s geographic location, experience level, skill set, training, licenses and certifications.\n\n\nOur Benefits: Global vision, local impact\n   \u2022 At OSTTRA, our benefits philosophy offers a market-competitive package that reflects our position as an industry leader. We want to ensure you feel valued, secure, and empowered wherever you are in the world.\n   \u2022 Our approach is built on three core pillars:\n   \u2022 Global foundations: We provide a baseline of excellence across all our offices, focusing on comprehensive Health & Wellness, Financial Security, and Work-Life Balance. No matter your location, you are part of a culture that prioritizes your holistic well-being.\n   \u2022 Locally tailored: We benchmark in each market to ensure our packages are genuinely competitive where you live and work.\n   \u2022 Flexibility and growth: We empower you to work in a way that suits your life. This includes a hybrid working model, generous leave policies, and a commitment to your continuous professional development.\n\nThe Trust employee ownership plan\nEvery employee at OSTTRA is an owner, and a member of The Trust, our employee ownership programme. Our distinct culture encourages colleagues to think and act like owners and raise the bar constantly. This plan reflects our belief that when we work together to build a stronger, more valuable organisation, then all colleagues should benefit from the value we create.\n\nAbout OSTTRA\n\nWe build and operate the infrastructure that the world\u2019s post-trade financial system runs on. Launched in 2021, we have unified more than 20 years of heritage and expertise from four industry leaders into a single, integrated business.\n\nToday,we operate a trusted network that connects thousands of market participants to streamline end-to-end workflows, from trade capture through portfolio optimisation.We translate industry change into workable process, engineering an open, intelligent ecosystem that removes friction and reduces risk for the global markets.\n\nOur distinct ownership culture is underpinned by four behaviours: boldness, curiosity, accountability, and collaboration. In 2025 we were acquired by KKR, one of the world\u2019s most successful private equity firms, and are on a journey of growth and impact.\n\nJoining our team now is a unique opportunity - you will help to shape the next generation of post-trade, transform shared infrastructure into shared benefit, and accelerate your own career. Learn more at www.osttra.com.\n\nEqual opportunity employer statement at OSTTRA\nWe are committed to fostering a connected and engaged workplace where all colleagues have access to opportunities based on their skills, experience, and contributions. Our hiring practices emphasise fairness, transparency, and merit, ensuring that we attract and retain the best talent. By valuing different perspectives and promoting a culture of respect and collaboration, we drive and operate the infrastructure that the world\u2019s post-trade financial system runs on","ClientSiteName":"Client Careers Site","ClientSiteXRefCode":"CANDIDATEPORTAL","CompanyName":"OSTTRA","ParentCompanyName":"OSTTRA","JobDetailsUrl":"https:\/\/jobs.dayforcehcm.com\/en-US\/osttrahcm\/CANDIDATEPORTAL\/jobs\/1192","ApplyUrl":"https:\/\/jobs.dayforcehcm.com\/en-US\/osttrahcm\/CANDIDATEPORTAL\/jobs\/1192\/apply","City":"New York","State":"NY","Country":"US","PostalCode":"","JobFamily":"Technology","DatePosted":"2026-08-31T00:00:00","LastUpdated":"2026-08-31T15:26:59.337","ReferenceNumber":1192,"CultureCode":"en-US","ParentRequisitionCode":182,"MinHiringRate":85000,"MaxHiringRate":100000,"JobType":0,"TravelRequired":0,"IsVirtualLocation":false},{"Title":"Client Services Lead (Optimization) ","Description":"Job Overview\n\n\nAbout the Role:\n\nThe team:\nThe role is responsible for coordinating and managing the regional triReduce-triBalance Client services team consisting of 5-6 team members. The role also involves most aspects of delivering the triReduce and triBalance cycles.\n\nResponsibilities and Impact:\nManage the regional triReduce-triBalance Client services team:\n   1. Coordinate the workflow for the different cycles of the team\n   2. Ensure all team members are conversant with the latest technical knowledge required to deliver the service and generate Unwind Proposals.\n   3. Coordinate activities of the team such as meetings, training, customer visits, etc. to ensure full support coverage for clients\n   4. Provide internal training for new and existing members of the team.\n   5. Participate in the regional recruiting process.\n   6. Ensure that the team get good feedback and support to evolve in their role, by holding formal and informal one-to-one meetings with each team member.\n   7. Strengthen the Osttra values by acting as a role model in the team.\n\nOversee Client services for regional clients\n   1. Ensure regional clients receive adequate training and support\n   2. Ensure regional clients derive maximum value from triReduce and triBalance. This is achieved through a combination of communication, support, training and escalation as appropriate.\n\nContribute to Global Client services organisation\n   1. The team leader is responsible for ensuring that the cycles are properly staffed in a reasonable amount of time prior to the cycle.\n   2. Work with Head of Client services and regional team leaders to ensure that work is done with a consistent global approach.\n   3. Liaise with and contribute to Client services activities in other regions.\n   4. Continuously improve internal processes with the objective to achieve a high degree of reliability of producing triReduce-triBalance cycles.\n   5. Provide feedback on market or client variables, which influence the timing of regional cycles, as well as the allocation of regional resources for the cycle team.\n\nWhat we\u2019re looking for:\nFundamental requirements:\n   1. Leadership \u2013 This role requires the ability to lead, organise and delegate successfully to the team of people working within the regional team.\n   2. Knowledge of the services \u2013 It is a key requirement to have a detailed understanding of the triReduce and triBalance services, how the services work, the problems they solve, the limitations and the flexibility of what can be done when using the services.\n   3. Communication \u2013 This role must be able to effectively communicate with our clients to quickly address any issues that may arise before they turn into real problems.\n   4. Financial Industry knowledge \u2013 This role shall be versed in the financial markets; processes related to trading and post execution and OTC derivatives products. Strong OTC product knowledge in terms of valuation and risk.\n   5. IT\/Technical \u2013 Solid technical knowledge of Osttra platforms. Good understanding of MySQL database structures and handling SQL queries. Basic understanding of Python programming\n\nThe location: New York, USA\n\nRight to work requirements:\nThis role is limited to persons with indefinite right to work in the United States.\n\nCompensation\/benefits information:\nThe anticipated base salary range for this position is $130,000 to $165,000. Final base salary for this role will be based on the individual\u2019s geographic location, experience level, skill set, training, licenses and certifications.\n\nOur Benefits: Global vision, local impact\nAt OSTTRA, our benefits philosophy offers a market-competitive package that reflects our position as an industry leader. We want to ensure you feel valued, secure, and empowered wherever you are in the world.\n\nOur approach is built on three core pillars:\n   \u2022 Global foundations: We provide a baseline of excellence across all our offices, focusing on comprehensive Health & Wellness, Financial Security, and Work-Life Balance. No matter your location, you are part of a culture that prioritizes your holistic well-being.\n   \u2022 Locally tailored: We benchmark in each market to ensure our packages are genuinely competitive where you live and work.\n   \u2022 Flexibility and growth: We empower you to work in a way that suits your life. This includes a hybrid working model, generous leave policies, and a commitment to your continuous professional development.\n\nThe Trust employee ownership plan\nEvery employee at OSTTRA is an owner, and a member of The Trust, our employee ownership programme. Our distinct culture encourages colleagues to think and act like owners and raise the bar constantly.\n\nThis plan reflects our belief that when we work together to build a stronger, more valuable organisation, then all colleagues should benefit from the value we create.\n\nAbout OSTTRA\nWe build and operate the infrastructure that the world\u2019s post-trade financial system runs on. Launched in 2021, we have unified more than 20 years of heritage and expertise from four industry leaders into a single, integrated business.\n\nToday, we operate a trusted network that connects thousands of market participants to streamline end-to-end workflows, from trade capture through portfolio optimisation.We translate industry change into workable process, engineering an open, intelligent ecosystem that removes friction and reduces risk for the global markets.\n\nOur distinct ownership culture is underpinned by four behaviours: boldness, curiosity, accountability, and collaboration. In 2025 we were acquired by KKR, one of the world\u2019s most successful private equity firms, and are on a journey of growth and impact.\nJoining our team now is a unique opportunity - you will help to shape the next generation of post-trade, transform shared infrastructure into shared benefit, and accelerate your own career. Learn more at www.osttra.com.\n\nEqual opportunity employer statement at OSTTRA:\nWe are committed to fostering a connected and engaged workplace where all colleagues have access to opportunities based on their skills, experience, and contributions. Our hiring practices emphasise fairness, transparency, and merit, ensuring that we attract and retain the best talent. By valuing different perspectives and promoting a culture of respect and collaboration, we drive and operate the infrastructure that the world\u2019s post-trade financial system runs on.\nThe location: New York, USA\n\nRight to work requirements:\nThis role is limited to persons with indefinite right to work in the United States.\n\nCompensation\/benefits information:\nThe anticipated base salary range for this position is $130,000 to $165,000. Final base salary for this role will be based on the individual\u2019s geographic location, experience level, skill set, training, licenses and certifications.\n\nOur Benefits: Global vision, local impact\nAt OSTTRA, our benefits philosophy offers a market-competitive package that reflects our position as an industry leader. We want to ensure you feel valued, secure, and empowered wherever you are in the world.\n\nOur approach is built on three core pillars:\n   \u2022 Global foundations: We provide a baseline of excellence across all our offices, focusing on comprehensive Health & Wellness, Financial Security, and Work-Life Balance. No matter your location, you are part of a culture that prioritizes your holistic well-being.\n   \u2022 Locally tailored: We benchmark in each market to ensure our packages are genuinely competitive where you live and work.\n   \u2022 Flexibility and growth: We empower you to work in a way that suits your life. This includes a hybrid working model, generous leave policies, and a commitment to your continuous professional development.\n\nThe Trust employee ownership plan\nEvery employee at OSTTRA is an owner, and a member of The Trust, our employee ownership programme. Our distinct culture encourages colleagues to think and act like owners and raise the bar constantly.\n\nThis plan reflects our belief that when we work together to build a stronger, more valuable organisation, then all colleagues should benefit from the value we create.\n\nAbout OSTTRA\nWe build and operate the infrastructure that the world\u2019s post-trade financial system runs on. Launched in 2021, we have unified more than 20 years of heritage and expertise from four industry leaders into a single, integrated business.\n\nToday, we operate a trusted network that connects thousands of market participants to streamline end-to-end workflows, from trade capture through portfolio optimisation.We translate industry change into workable process, engineering an open, intelligent ecosystem that removes friction and reduces risk for the global markets.\n\nOur distinct ownership culture is underpinned by four behaviours: boldness, curiosity, accountability, and collaboration. In 2025 we were acquired by KKR, one of the world\u2019s most successful private equity firms, and are on a journey of growth and impact.\nJoining our team now is a unique opportunity - you will help to shape the next generation of post-trade, transform shared infrastructure into shared benefit, and accelerate your own career. Learn more at www.osttra.com.\n\nEqual opportunity employer statement at OSTTRA:\nWe are committed to fostering a connected and engaged workplace where all colleagues have access to opportunities based on their skills, experience, and contributions. Our hiring practices emphasise fairness, transparency, and merit, ensuring that we attract and retain the best talent. By valuing different perspectives and promoting a culture of respect and collaboration, we drive and operate the infrastructure that the world\u2019s post-trade financial system runs on.","ClientSiteName":"Client Careers Site","ClientSiteXRefCode":"CANDIDATEPORTAL","CompanyName":"OSTTRA","ParentCompanyName":"OSTTRA","JobDetailsUrl":"https:\/\/jobs.dayforcehcm.com\/en-US\/osttrahcm\/CANDIDATEPORTAL\/jobs\/1194","ApplyUrl":"https:\/\/jobs.dayforcehcm.com\/en-US\/osttrahcm\/CANDIDATEPORTAL\/jobs\/1194\/apply","City":"New York","State":"NY","Country":"US","PostalCode":"","JobFamily":"Optimisation","DatePosted":"2026-09-01T00:00:00","LastUpdated":"2026-09-01T15:47:32.07","ReferenceNumber":1194,"CultureCode":"en-US","ParentRequisitionCode":244,"JobType":0,"TravelRequired":0,"IsVirtualLocation":false},{"Title":"Client Services Analyst","Description":"Job Overview\n\n\nAbout the Role:\nThe team:\nThe Senior Client Services Analyst is dedicated to supporting our new and existing customers to ensure they receive the maximum benefit of their OSTTRA services. This position focuses on providing application and technical support for our global client base. The ideal candidate will possess strong client focus, excellent communication and organizational skills. The role requires working directly with OSTTRA customers as well as internal projects, onboarding, and development teams. This is a client-facing role; as such, the ideal candidate works well under pressure while keeping client needs paramount. The primary purpose of this role is to contribute as a member of the support team in New York, align with the global approach, optimize processes, and help deliver top level support to our clients.\n\nResponsibilities and Impact:\n   \u2022 Act as a support representative for key clients, building and maintaining strong relationships.\n   \u2022 Monitor Salesforce queues to ensure all cases are addressed promptly and professionally.\n   \u2022 Troubleshoot and resolve complex client issues, ensuring high levels of client satisfaction.\n   \u2022 Develop an in-depth understanding of the fintech platform, products, and services.\n   \u2022 Align with global strategies and contribute to a unified client service approach.\n   \u2022 Identify and recommend process enhancements to improve client experience and operational efficiency.\n   \u2022 Collaborate with internal teams to ensure timely and efficient problem resolution.\n\nWhat we\u2019re looking for:\nFundamental requirement:\n   \u2022 1-3 Years Experience in Financial technology services and\/or banking.\n   \u2022 BA\/BS in Business, Finance, Economics or Computer Science preferred.\n   \u2022 Excellent communications skills and experience dealing with clients at various levels.\n   \u2022 Knowledge of trade life cycles, OSTTRA services (OSTTRA Connect for Rates, Equity & Repo \u2013 formerly known as Markitwire is preferred) or other related post trade processing platforms, and middle and back office experience preferred.\n   \u2022 Ability to work under pressure to resolve client issues including those which are novel to the team.\n   \u2022 Ability to work flexible hours \/ shifts.\n   \u2022 Ability to work both independently and within a team to follow through on issues from beginning to end.\nThe location: New York, USA\nRight to work requirements:\nThis role is limited to persons with indefinite right to work in the United States.\nCompensation\/benefits information:\nThe anticipated base salary range for this position is $70.000 to $85,000. Final base salary for this role will be based on the individual\u2019s geographic location, experience level, skill set, training, licenses and certifications.\nOur Benefits: Global vision, local impact\nAt OSTTRA, our benefits philosophy offers a market-competitive package that reflects our position as an industry leader. We want to ensure you feel valued, secure, and empowered wherever you are in the world.\nOur approach is built on three core pillars:\n   \u2022 Global foundations: We provide a baseline of excellence across all our offices, focusing on comprehensive Health & Wellness, Financial Security, and Work-Life Balance. No matter your location, you are part of a culture that prioritizes your holistic well-being.\n   \u2022 Locally tailored: We benchmark in each market to ensure our packages are genuinely competitive where you live and work.\n   \u2022 Flexibility and growth: We empower you to work in a way that suits your life. This includes a hybrid working model, generous leave policies, and a commitment to your continuous professional development.\n\nThe Trust employee ownership plan\nEvery employee at OSTTRA is an owner, and a member of The Trust, our employee ownership programme. Our distinct culture encourages colleagues to think and act like owners and raise the bar constantly.\nThis plan reflects our belief that when we work together to build a stronger, more valuable organisation, then all colleagues should benefit from the value we create.\nAbout OSTTRA\nWe build and operate the infrastructure that the world\u2019s post-trade financial system runs on. Launched in 2021, we have unified more than 20 years of heritage and expertise from four industry leaders into a single, integrated business.\nToday,we operate a trusted network that connects thousands of market participants to streamline end-to-end workflows, from trade capture through portfolio optimisation.We translate industry change into workable process, engineering an open, intelligent ecosystem that removes friction and reduces risk for the global markets.\n\nOur distinct ownership culture is underpinned by four behaviours: boldness, curiosity, accountability, and collaboration. In 2025 we were acquired by KKR, one of the world\u2019s most successful private equity firms, and are on a journey of growth and impact.\nJoining our team now is a unique opportunity - you will help to shape the next generation of post-trade, transform shared infrastructure into shared benefit, and accelerate your own career. Learn more at www.osttra.com.\nEqual opportunity employer statement at OSTTRA:\nWe are committed to fostering a connected and engaged workplace where all colleagues have access to opportunities based on their skills, experience, and contributions. Our hiring practices emphasise fairness, transparency, and merit, ensuring that we attract and retain the best talent. By valuing different perspectives and promoting a culture of respect and collaboration, we drive and operate the infrastructure that the world\u2019s post-trade financial system runs on.","ClientSiteName":"Client Careers Site","ClientSiteXRefCode":"CANDIDATEPORTAL","CompanyName":"OSTTRA","ParentCompanyName":"OSTTRA","JobDetailsUrl":"https:\/\/jobs.dayforcehcm.com\/en-US\/osttrahcm\/CANDIDATEPORTAL\/jobs\/1207","ApplyUrl":"https:\/\/jobs.dayforcehcm.com\/en-US\/osttrahcm\/CANDIDATEPORTAL\/jobs\/1207\/apply","City":"New York","State":"NY","Country":"US","PostalCode":"","DatePosted":"2026-09-02T00:00:00","LastUpdated":"2026-09-02T22:36:29.183","ReferenceNumber":1207,"CultureCode":"en-US","ParentRequisitionCode":258,"JobType":0,"TravelRequired":0,"IsVirtualLocation":false},{"Title":"Business Analyst","Description":"Job Overview\n\n\nAbout the Role:\nThe team: Our Engineering team develops and maintains modern, cloud-based applications and AI-powered solutions that support global business operations. Team members collaborate across Product, Architecture, QA, and DevOps functions to build reliable, secure, and scalable solutions. The team embraces agile delivery practices and encourages continuous learning, innovation, and professional growth.\n\nResponsibilities and impact:\nWe build a platform that replaces manual month-end NAV reconciliation and investor income allocation processes for hedge fund operations teams. You will be the bridge between our fund clients and our engineering team \u2014 understanding how each client's fund accounting operations work, translating that into precise specifications, and ensuring the platform delivers correct financial outcomes. This is a client-facing role.\nKey Responsibilities\n   \u2022 Lead UAT and Stakeholder Engagement: Collaborate directly with fund operations teams during month-end to observe reconciliation and allocation workflows, conduct feature demonstrations, and drive user acceptance testing (UAT).\n   \u2022 Own End-to-End Validation: Manage the full feature delivery lifecycle, ensuring that calculation results are fully verified and confirmed as accurate by the client before deeming a feature complete.\n   \u2022 Drive Hands-on Analysis: Act as a forward-deployed business analyst by drafting comprehensive specifications, exploring complex calculation edge cases, and proactively contributing to technical solutions.\n   \u2022 Collaborate with Engineering: Partner closely with engineering teams to define and refine data models and calculation logic, ensuring business requirements translate into robust technical implementations.\n   \u2022 Execute Technical Validation: Perform hands-on data validation and analysis by utilizing SQL and other technical tools to verify system outputs and ensure data integrity.\n   \u2022 Integrate AI-Augmented Workflows: Leverage AI assistants to accelerate analysis and process efficiency, maintaining a curiosity-driven approach to pushing the boundaries of what is possible with new technology.\n\nWhat we\u2019re looking for:\nYou will have 5-8 years of experience with fluency in fund accounting: NAV calculation, trial balances, portfolio valuations, realized vs. unrealized P&L, management and performance fee waterfalls, hurdle rates, high water marks, investor allocations, capital activity processing (subscriptions, redemptions, transfers), equalisation mechanics, and accounting period controls.\nRequired Skills\n   \u2022 Domain Expertise and Accounting Rigor: Deep knowledge of fund accounting and administration systems, utilizing strong analytical and problem-solving skills to break down complex scenarios, identify edge cases, and maintain absolute precision in calculations to prevent compounding errors across periods.\n   \u2022 Business Analysis and Delivery: Proven proficiency in requirements elicitation\u2014including structured interviews, process flows, and defining acceptance criteria\u2014combined with a proactive, ownership-driven mindset to drive deliverables to completion without needing prompting.\n   \u2022 Client Relations and Results Focus: Exceptional client-facing confidence in presenting methodologies and fielding difficult questions when results deviate, with an outcome-driven mindset that measures success strictly by the accuracy of financial results rather than completed process steps.\n   \u2022 Technical Acumen and AI Integration: Strong technical literacy, including SQL for data analysis and validation, paired with a genuine appetite for integrating and utilizing AI-augmented workflows daily to accelerate work and contribute directly to technical solutions.\n\nPreferred Skills\n   \u2022 Fund Accounting & Operations Expertise: Deep functional expertise in fund accounting operations, encompassing complex fee calculation methodologies (management fee accrual, incentive fees with hurdle and HWM, equalisation, crystallisation, series\/lot accounting), investor reporting, capital activity workflows, multi-currency fund structures, and comprehensive reconciliation workflows, including managing tolerance thresholds, variance investigation, and resolution processes.\n   \u2022 AI-Augmented Technical Skills: Demonstrated hands-on practical experience utilizing AI assistants (e.g., Copilot, ChatGPT) as essential tools to accelerate and optimize professional workflows, specifically applying them to complex financial analysis, specification writing, and data exploration tasks.\n\nThe location: Gurgaon,India\n\nOur Benefits: Global vision, local impact\nAt OSTTRA, our benefits philosophy offers a market-competitive package that reflects our position as an industry leader. We want to ensure you feel valued, secure, and empowered wherever you are in the world.\nOur approach is built on three core pillars:\n   \u2022 Global foundations: We provide a baseline of excellence across all our offices, focusing on comprehensive Health & Wellness, Financial Security, and Work-Life Balance. No matter your location, you are part of a culture that prioritizes your holistic well-being.\n   \u2022 Locally tailored: We benchmark in each market to ensure our packages are genuinely competitive where you live and work.\n   \u2022 Flexibility and growth: We empower you to work in a way that suits your life. This includes a hybrid working model, generous leave policies, and a commitment to your continuous professional development.\n\n\nThe Trust employee ownership plan\nEvery employee at OSTTRA is an owner, and a member of The Trust, our employee ownership programme. Our distinct culture encourages colleagues to think and act like owners and raise the bar constantly. This plan reflects our belief that when we work together to build a stronger, more valuable organisation, then all colleagues should benefit from the value we create.\n\nAbout OSTTRA\nWe build and operate the infrastructure that the world\u2019s post-trade financial system runs on. Launched in 2021, we have unified more than 20 years of heritage and expertise from four industry leaders into a single, integrated business.\nToday,we operate a trusted network that connects thousands of market participants to streamline end-to-end workflows, from trade capture through portfolio optimisation.We translate industry change into workable process, engineering an open, intelligent ecosystem that removes friction and reduces risk for the global markets.\nOur distinct ownership culture is underpinned by four behaviours: boldness, curiosity, accountability, and collaboration. In 2025 we were acquired by KKR, one of the world\u2019s most successful private equity firms, and are on a journey of growth and impact.\nJoining our team now is a unique opportunity - you will help to shape the next generation of post-trade, transform shared infrastructure into shared benefit, and accelerate your own career. Learn more atwww.osttra.com.\nEqual opportunity employer statement at OSTTRA\nWe are committed to fostering a connected and engaged workplace where all colleagues have access to opportunities based on their skills, experience, and contributions. Our hiring practices emphasise fairness, transparency, and merit, ensuring that we attract and retain the best talent. By valuing different perspectives and promoting a culture of respect and collaboration, we drive and operate the infrastructure that the world\u2019s post-trade financial system runs on.","ClientSiteName":"Client Careers Site","ClientSiteXRefCode":"CANDIDATEPORTAL","CompanyName":"OSTTRA","ParentCompanyName":"OSTTRA","JobDetailsUrl":"https:\/\/jobs.dayforcehcm.com\/en-US\/osttrahcm\/CANDIDATEPORTAL\/jobs\/1226","ApplyUrl":"https:\/\/jobs.dayforcehcm.com\/en-US\/osttrahcm\/CANDIDATEPORTAL\/jobs\/1226\/apply","City":"Gurugram","State":"HR","Country":"IN","PostalCode":"","DatePosted":"2026-09-14T20:30:00","LastUpdated":"2026-09-15T11:32:14.9","ReferenceNumber":1226,"CultureCode":"en-US","ParentRequisitionCode":276,"JobType":0,"TravelRequired":0,"IsVirtualLocation":false},{"Title":"Information Security Engineer (GRC)","Description":"Job Overview\n\n\nAbout the Role:\nThe team:\nThe Information Security team is responsible for security controls relating to protecting information in all formats. We maintain a number of policies and an Information Security Management System which dictates how infosec is integrated into processes as well as tools and technical controls to directly protect against cyber security threats.\n\nResponsibilities and impact:\nWe are seeking a dedicated and collaborative Information Security Engineer to join our growing Governance, Risk, and Compliance (GRC) team. In this role, you will play a pivotal part in maintaining, maturing, and auditing our information security management framework.\nThe ideal candidate has 3\u20135 years of direct experience within an InfoSec GRC function and thrives in a team-oriented environment. You will be responsible for ensuring our policies remain up-to-date, driving our ISO 27001 certification lifecycle, and executing core compliance operations like user access reviews, exception management, and security awareness programs.\n\nKey Responsibilities\nGovernance & ISO 27001 Management\n   \u2022 ISMS Governance: Manage and maintain our ISO 27001 Information Security Management System (ISMS) to ensure continuous compliance.\n   \u2022 Audit Facilitation: Lead internal security audits and act as a point of contact for external certification audits.\n   \u2022 Policy Management: Regularly review, update, and draft information security policies, standards, and procedures to align with evolving regulatory landscapes and business needs.\n\nGRC Operations & Risk Management\n   \u2022 Access Governance: Coordinate and oversee periodic user access reviews across critical systems.\n   \u2022 Exception Management: Evaluate, log, and monitor security policy exceptions, ensuring compensating controls are effectively implemented and tracked.\n   \u2022 Risk Culture: Administer the company-wide security awareness training program and orchestrate routine phishing simulations to strengthen our human firewall.\n\nCollaboration & Communication\n   \u2022 Partner closely with cross-functional teams (IT, Legal, HR, and Engineering) to embed security compliance into daily operations.\n   \u2022 Translate complex compliance requirements into actionable, easy-to-understand guidance for non-technical stakeholders.\n\n\nWhat we\u2019re looking for:\nRequired Experience & Skills\n   \u2022 Experience: 3\u20135 years of proven experience specifically within an Information Security GRC role.I\n   \u2022 ISO 27001 Expertise: Hands-on experience managing an ISO 27001 ISMS, including active participation in both internal and external certification audits.\n   \u2022 Core GRC Competencies: Direct experience executing user access reviews, phishing simulations, security training, and policy exception workflows.\n   \u2022 Communication: Exceptional verbal and written communication skills, with the ability to document clear policies and present findings to various business units.\n   \u2022 Soft Skills: A strong team player with a highly collaborative mindset, excellent problem-solving abilities, and a proactive approach to security culture.\n\nPreferred Qualifications (Nice-to-Have)\n   \u2022 Relevant industry certifications (e.g., ISO 27001 Internal\/Lead Auditor, CISA, CRISC, Security+, or CISM).\n   \u2022 Experience with the ISO 42001 AIMS standard.\n   \u2022 Experience utilizing GRC automation platforms\/tools.\n\n\nThe location: Gurgaon,India\n\nOur Benefits: Global vision, local impact\nAt OSTTRA, our benefits philosophy offers a market-competitive package that reflects our position as an industry leader. We want to ensure you feel valued, secure, and empowered wherever you are in the world.\nOur approach is built on three core pillars:\n   \u2022 Global foundations: We provide a baseline of excellence across all our offices, focusing on comprehensive Health & Wellness, Financial Security, and Work-Life Balance. No matter your location, you are part of a culture that prioritizes your holistic well-being.\n   \u2022 Locally tailored: We benchmark in each market to ensure our packages are genuinely competitive where you live and work.\n   \u2022 Flexibility and growth: We empower you to work in a way that suits your life. This includes a hybrid working model, generous leave policies, and a commitment to your continuous professional development.\n\n\nThe Trust employee ownership plan\nEvery employee at OSTTRA is an owner, and a member of The Trust, our employee ownership programme. Our distinct culture encourages colleagues to think and act like owners and raise the bar constantly. This plan reflects our belief that when we work together to build a stronger, more valuable organisation, then all colleagues should benefit from the value we create.\n\nAbout OSTTRA\nWe build and operate the infrastructure that the world\u2019s post-trade financial system runs on. Launched in 2021, we have unified more than 20 years of heritage and expertise from four industry leaders into a single, integrated business.\nToday,we operate a trusted network that connects thousands of market participants to streamline end-to-end workflows, from trade capture through portfolio optimisation.We translate industry change into workable process, engineering an open, intelligent ecosystem that removes friction and reduces risk for the global markets.\nOur distinct ownership culture is underpinned by four behaviours: boldness, curiosity, accountability, and collaboration. In 2025 we were acquired by KKR, one of the world\u2019s most successful private equity firms, and are on a journey of growth and impact.\nJoining our team now is a unique opportunity - you will help to shape the next generation of post-trade, transform shared infrastructure into shared benefit, and accelerate your own career. Learn more atwww.osttra.com.\nEqual opportunity employer statement at OSTTRA\nWe are committed to fostering a connected and engaged workplace where all colleagues have access to opportunities based on their skills, experience, and contributions. Our hiring practices emphasise fairness, transparency, and merit, ensuring that we attract and retain the best talent. By valuing different perspectives and promoting a culture of respect and collaboration, we drive and operate the infrastructure that the world\u2019s post-trade financial system runs on.","ClientSiteName":"Client Careers Site","ClientSiteXRefCode":"CANDIDATEPORTAL","CompanyName":"OSTTRA","ParentCompanyName":"OSTTRA","JobDetailsUrl":"https:\/\/jobs.dayforcehcm.com\/en-US\/osttrahcm\/CANDIDATEPORTAL\/jobs\/1230","ApplyUrl":"https:\/\/jobs.dayforcehcm.com\/en-US\/osttrahcm\/CANDIDATEPORTAL\/jobs\/1230\/apply","City":"Gurugram","State":"HR","Country":"IN","PostalCode":"","JobFamily":"Technology","EmploymentIndicator":"Regular","DatePosted":"2026-09-14T20:30:00","LastUpdated":"2026-09-15T11:46:03.18","ReferenceNumber":1230,"CultureCode":"en-US","ParentRequisitionCode":172,"JobType":0,"TravelRequired":0,"IsVirtualLocation":false},{"Title":"Customer Success & Relationship Management","Description":"Job Overview\n\n\nAbout the Role:\nThe team:\nAt OSTTRA, we are passionate about our clients and are looking for a Customer Success Representative ready to join our growing global team. The successful candidate will be a dedicated customer advocate who possesses excellent communication skills, can autonomously manage complex issues, and drive maximum value and success for existing clients.This role will focus on the overall post-sales relationship with our strategic and new customers. This includes growing adoption, customer education, and identifying improvement opportunities while maintaining high levels of satisfaction. For more regarding OSTTRA, please visit:www.osttra.com\nResponsibilities and impact:\nOSTTRA plays a critical role in supporting global financial markets, connecting thousands of counterparties on our multi-asset networks that underpin the post-trade lifecycle from trade capture, through portfolio optimization, to clearing and settlement. Our customers include banks, hedge funds, asset managers, central banks, regulators, auditors, fund administrators, and insurance companies. Our products and services have become deeply embedded in the systems and workflows of many of our customers. We have a track record of innovation, leveraging leading technologies, industry expertise, and strong relationships with market participants.\nIn this role, you'll be instrumental in ensuring our customers achieve their desired outcomes and maximize the value from their OSTTRA solutions. Your key responsibilities will include:\n   \u2022 Proactive Customer Engagement: Develop and maintain strong, long-lasting relationships with a portfolio of strategic and new customers, serving as their primary point of contact post-sale.\n   \u2022 Driving Adoption & Value: Guide customers through onboarding, training, and ongoing engagement to ensure full utilization and adoption of OSTTRA's platforms and services.\n   \u2022 Strategic Account Growth: Identify opportunities for expanded product usage and collaborate with the sales team on potential upsell and cross-sell initiatives.\n   \u2022 Customer Advocacy & Feedback: Collect, analyze, and communicate customer feedback to internal product and engineering teams, actively contributing to product development and improvements.\n   \u2022 Issue Resolution & Escalation: Act as a central point of contact for customer inquiries and complex issues, coordinating with support, product, and technical teams to ensure timely and effective resolution.\n   \u2022 Product Expertise: Become a subject matter expert on OSTTRA's platforms, providing guidance and best practices to customers.\n   \u2022 Performance Monitoring: Utilize data and analytics to monitor customer health, usage patterns, and identify areas for intervention or growth.\nWhat we\u2019re looking for:\nFundamental requirement:\n   \u2022 Financial Market Knowledge: A sound understanding of financial markets and market participants. Knowledge of Collateral Management and Uncleared Margin Rules will be a huge advantage\n   \u2022 Experience: Over 5 years in a related function with direct customer advocacy and engagement experience in software post-sales or professional services.\n   \u2022 Platform Familiarity: Experience with triResolve, triResolve Margin, or similar platform.\n   \u2022 Language Fluency: Fluency in English is required; one or more additional languages is a plus.\n   \u2022 Client Services Orientation: Strong listening, critical thinking, analytical skills, and a high degree of empathy.\n Additional preferred requirements:\n   \u2022 Team Player: An active team player who thrives in a multi-tasking environment, can adjust priorities on the fly, and maintains strong attention to detail.\n   \u2022 Data Acumen: Experience and\/or interest in data analytics tools and utilizing data to monitor customer usage and identify adoption opportunities is a plus.\n   \u2022 Problem-Solving: Demonstrated ability to analyze complex situations, identify root causes, and propose effective solutions.\n   \u2022 Time Management & Organization: Capacity to manage multiple priorities and deadlines effectively in a fast-paced environment.\n   \u2022 Self-Motivated & Proactive: A driven individual who takes initiative and anticipates customer needs.\n The location: Tokya, Japan","ClientSiteName":"Client Careers Site","ClientSiteXRefCode":"CANDIDATEPORTAL","CompanyName":"OSTTRA","ParentCompanyName":"OSTTRA","JobDetailsUrl":"https:\/\/jobs.dayforcehcm.com\/en-US\/osttrahcm\/CANDIDATEPORTAL\/jobs\/1234","ApplyUrl":"https:\/\/jobs.dayforcehcm.com\/en-US\/osttrahcm\/CANDIDATEPORTAL\/jobs\/1234\/apply","City":"","State":"","Country":"JP","PostalCode":"","JobFamily":"Customer Success & Relationship Management","EmploymentIndicator":"Regular","DatePosted":"2026-09-15T20:30:00","LastUpdated":"2026-09-16T07:36:09.447","ReferenceNumber":1234,"CultureCode":"en-US","ParentRequisitionCode":149,"JobType":0,"TravelRequired":0,"IsVirtualLocation":false},{"Title":"Sr Product Analysis & Design Specialist","Description":"Job Overview\n\n\nAbout the Role:\nThe team: The OSTTRA Product team comprises Capital Markets professionals dedicated to designing, building, and safeguarding the applications that power our network. Leveraging contemporary microservices and cloud-based architectures, we manage a sophisticated landscape of high-performance, compute-intensive technology.\n\nResponsibilities and impact:\nOSTTRA is currently seeking a Technical Product Manager to support our FX & Securities Platforms, ensuring seamless trade processing, regulatory compliance, and settlement across systems that handle over 100 million messages daily.\nIn this role, you will collaborate with agile cross-functional teams\u2014including product, development, QA, and operations\u2014across global locations like India, Singapore, Tokyo, New York, and London. The ideal candidate brings strong analytical, organizational, and communication skills, a process-oriented mindset, and the ability to build robust internal and external relationships with clients, clearing houses, venues, and trade repositories in a fast-paced environment.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n   \u2022 Coordination with stakeholders for requirements elicitation to meet customer\/market expectations\n   \u2022 Ensure alignment among the business, tech and other teams\n   \u2022 Prioritization of future features and functionalities, to create product roadmap\n   \u2022 Coordinate and communicate the product roadmap with all stakeholders and ensure its delivery\n   \u2022 Analyze and represent the requirements in epics\/stories, usecases, and define acceptance criteria for each functionality towards delivery\n   \u2022 Support other teams in analysing production issues, client queries\n   \u2022 Support UAT (internal and client teams) from functional point of view and incorporate feedback in future releases of OTC & ETD derivatives terms and principles\n\nWhat we\u2019re looking for:\nFundamental requirement:\n   \u2022 Post graduate \u2013 Bachelor\u2019s or Master\u2019s Degree preferred in related field\n   \u2022 7+ years of relevant professional experience\n   \u2022 Demonstrate experience of working in a product management environment\n   \u2022 Strong Analytical & Communication skills\n   \u2022 Good knowledge of requirements elicitation, structured analysis, requirement documentation, stakeholder management, use case and user story definition and other business analysis techniques\n   \u2022 Commercial awareness and financial services experience\n\nAdditional preferred requirements:\n   \u2022 Understanding of OTC & ETD derivatives terms and principles\n   \u2022 Experience working as a business analyst in an agile scrum team\n   \u2022 Familiarity with financials asset classes and trading lifecycle\n   \u2022 Understanding of FIX\/FpML or other messaging formats or protocols\n   \u2022 Commercial awareness and financial services experience\n\nThe location: Gurgaon,India\n\nOur Benefits: Global vision, local impact\nAt OSTTRA, our benefits philosophy offers a market-competitive package that reflects our position as an industry leader. We want to ensure you feel valued, secure, and empowered wherever you are in the world.\nOur approach is built on three core pillars:\n   \u2022 Global foundations: We provide a baseline of excellence across all our offices, focusing on comprehensive Health & Wellness, Financial Security, and Work-Life Balance. No matter your location, you are part of a culture that prioritizes your holistic well-being.\n   \u2022 Locally tailored: We benchmark in each market to ensure our packages are genuinely competitive where you live and work.\n   \u2022 Flexibility and growth: We empower you to work in a way that suits your life. This includes a hybrid working model, generous leave policies, and a commitment to your continuous professional development.\n\n\nThe Trust employee ownership plan\nEvery employee at OSTTRA is an owner, and a member of The Trust, our employee ownership programme. Our distinct culture encourages colleagues to think and act like owners and raise the bar constantly. This plan reflects our belief that when we work together to build a stronger, more valuable organisation, then all colleagues should benefit from the value we create.\n\nAbout OSTTRA\nWe build and operate the infrastructure that the world\u2019s post-trade financial system runs on. Launched in 2021, we have unified more than 20 years of heritage and expertise from four industry leaders into a single, integrated business.\nToday,we operate a trusted network that connects thousands of market participants to streamline end-to-end workflows, from trade capture through portfolio optimisation.We translate industry change into workable process, engineering an open, intelligent ecosystem that removes friction and reduces risk for the global markets.\nOur distinct ownership culture is underpinned by four behaviours: boldness, curiosity, accountability, and collaboration. In 2025 we were acquired by KKR, one of the world\u2019s most successful private equity firms, and are on a journey of growth and impact.\nJoining our team now is a unique opportunity - you will help to shape the next generation of post-trade, transform shared infrastructure into shared benefit, and accelerate your own career. Learn more atwww.osttra.com.\n\nEqual opportunity employer statement at OSTTRA\nWe are committed to fostering a connected and engaged workplace where all colleagues have access to opportunities based on their skills, experience, and contributions. Our hiring practices emphasise fairness, transparency, and merit, ensuring that we attract and retain the best talent. By valuing different perspectives and promoting a culture of respect and collaboration, we drive and operate the infrastructure that the world\u2019s post-trade financial system runs on.","ClientSiteName":"Client Careers Site","ClientSiteXRefCode":"CANDIDATEPORTAL","CompanyName":"OSTTRA","ParentCompanyName":"OSTTRA","JobDetailsUrl":"https:\/\/jobs.dayforcehcm.com\/en-US\/osttrahcm\/CANDIDATEPORTAL\/jobs\/1238","ApplyUrl":"https:\/\/jobs.dayforcehcm.com\/en-US\/osttrahcm\/CANDIDATEPORTAL\/jobs\/1238\/apply","City":"Gurugram","State":"HR","Country":"IN","PostalCode":"","JobFamily":"Product","EmploymentIndicator":"Regular","DatePosted":"2026-09-20T20:30:00","LastUpdated":"2026-09-21T14:02:57.247","ReferenceNumber":1238,"CultureCode":"en-US","ParentRequisitionCode":268,"JobType":0,"TravelRequired":0,"IsVirtualLocation":false},{"Title":"Senior Client Services Associate ","Description":"Job Overview\n\n\nThe team:\n\nThe Client Services team provides primary-level problem resolution, technical application support, and account management to current and potential clients. In this role, you will lead client onboarding, troubleshoot operational issues, drive engagement on new initiatives, and optimize internal workflows to ensure our global client base receives maximum benefit from OSTTRA services.\n\nResponsibilities and Impact:\n   \u2022 Client Relationship & Account Management: Manage key client accounts and interface directly with senior stakeholders. Serve as a primary point of contact for clients, leading account onboarding, managing ongoing relationships, and driving client engagement across core initiatives.\n   \u2022 Issue Resolution & Support: Troubleshoot complex, novel technical issues under pressure and resolve daily operational, customer-related, and technical application issues across all asset classes and services (Core\/TM\/triCalc\/IMEM), maintaining Salesforce queues to ensure prompt resolution.\n   \u2022 Team Guidance & Quality Control: Serve as a dedicated technical resource and mentor for junior team member. Conduct checks on Analyst work to ensure quality, answer process questions, and act as an internal escalation point.\n   \u2022 Product & Process Optimization: Partner with CD&S and BLM teams on new initiatives, document firm enhancement requests, create product development tickets, and recommend process improvements to increase operational efficiency.\n   \u2022 Special Projects & Strategy: Analyze client service metrics to identify trends, validate functionality requirements with clients, and contribute to special projects, pilots, or global strategy alignments.\n\nWhat we\u2019re looking for:\nFundamental requirements:\n   \u2022 Industry Knowledge: Deep understanding of front, middle, and back-office operations, trade lifecycles, and where OSTTRA fits within the post-trade financial ecosystem.\n   \u2022 Product Expertise: 5+ years of experience in financial technology services and\/or banking; BA\/BS in Business, Finance, Economics, or Computer Science preferred). Hands-on product experience with OTC and Exchange Traded derivatives and their respective markets.\n   \u2022 Technical Skills (Preferred for Senior level): Familiarity with database tools, common transport protocols (MQ, Email, FTP, SFTP), and operating systems (Windows, Unix, Linux)\n   \u2022 Communication & Problem Solving: Strong client-facing skills, ability to manage multiple stakeholders, interpret data, and work both independently and collaboratively under pressure.\n\nThe location: New York, USA\n\nRight to work requirements:\nThis role is limited to persons with indefinite right to work in the United States.\n\nCompensation\/benefits information:\nThe anticipated base salary range for these positions is $95,000 to $127,000. Final base salary will be based on the individual\u2019s geographic location, experience level, skill set, training, licenses, and certifications.\nOur Benefits: Global vision, local impact\nAt OSTTRA, our benefits philosophy offers a market-competitive package that reflects our position as an industry leader. We want to ensure you feel valued, secure, and empowered wherever you are in the world.\nOur approach is built on three core pillars:\n   \u2022 Global foundations: We provide a baseline of excellence across all our offices, focusing on comprehensive Health & Wellness, Financial Security, and Work-Life Balance. No matter your location, you are part of a culture that prioritizes your holistic well-being.\n   \u2022 Locally tailored: We benchmark in each market to ensure our packages are genuinely competitive where you live and work.\n   \u2022 Flexibility and growth: We empower you to work in a way that suits your life. This includes a hybrid working model, generous leave policies, and a commitment to your continuous professional development.\n\nThe Trust employee ownership plan\nEvery employee at OSTTRA is an owner, and a member of The Trust, our employee ownership programme. Our distinct culture encourages colleagues to think and act like owners and raise the bar constantly.\nThis plan reflects our belief that when we work together to build a stronger, more valuable organisation, then all colleagues should benefit from the value we create.\nAbout OSTTRA\nWe build and operate the infrastructure that the world\u2019s post-trade financial system runs on. Launched in 2021, we have unified more than 20 years of heritage and expertise from four industry leaders into a single, integrated business.\nToday,we operate a trusted network that connects thousands of market participants to streamline end-to-end workflows, from trade capture through portfolio optimisation.We translate industry change into workable process, engineering an open, intelligent ecosystem that removes friction and reduces risk for the global markets.\n\nOur distinct ownership culture is underpinned by four behaviours: boldness, curiosity, accountability, and collaboration. In 2025 we were acquired by KKR, one of the world\u2019s most successful private equity firms, and are on a journey of growth and impact.\nJoining our team now is a unique opportunity - you will help to shape the next generation of post-trade, transform shared infrastructure into shared benefit, and accelerate your own career. Learn more at www.osttra.com.\nEqual opportunity employer statement at OSTTRA:\nWe are committed to fostering a connected and engaged workplace where all colleagues have access to opportunities based on their skills, experience, and contributions. Our hiring practices emphasise fairness, transparency, and merit, ensuring that we attract and retain the best talent. By valuing different perspectives and promoting a culture of respect and collaboration, we drive and operate the infrastructure that the world\u2019s post-trade financial system runs on.","ClientSiteName":"Client Careers Site","ClientSiteXRefCode":"CANDIDATEPORTAL","CompanyName":"OSTTRA","ParentCompanyName":"OSTTRA","JobDetailsUrl":"https:\/\/jobs.dayforcehcm.com\/en-US\/osttrahcm\/CANDIDATEPORTAL\/jobs\/1241","ApplyUrl":"https:\/\/jobs.dayforcehcm.com\/en-US\/osttrahcm\/CANDIDATEPORTAL\/jobs\/1241\/apply","City":"New York","State":"NY","Country":"US","PostalCode":"","DatePosted":"2026-10-01T00:00:00","LastUpdated":"2026-10-01T14:59:57.66","ReferenceNumber":1241,"CultureCode":"en-US","ParentRequisitionCode":270,"JobType":0,"TravelRequired":0,"IsVirtualLocation":false},{"Title":"Software Engineer","Description":"Job Overview\n\n\nAbout the Role:\nThe team:\nThe development team is based in Stockholm and consists of 22 highly skilled individuals with diverse backgrounds, each engineer playing their unique part in serving our global customer base. Everyone on the team shares the responsibility of meeting all functional and non-functional requirements, and you\u2019ll find that the team decisions cover not only business-related improvements but also a wide variety of technical topics such as architectural styles, Kubernetes operators, deployment pipelines, data locality strategies, observability solutions, frontend frameworks and much much more. The team is responsible for a complex system requiring a lot of collaboration within the team and with other parts of the technology organisation and we value learning from each other in order to continuously improve ourselves and the user experience.\n\nResponsibilities and impact:\n\nOSTTRA is a FinTech company at the heart of the global financial system, dedicated to building the future of post-trade. OSTTRA Resolve is our post-trade service that offers an automated trade portfolio reconciliation workflow. Improvement of OSTTRA Resolve has far-reaching effects in this important segment of the financial industry, not only through expanded capabilities of other integrated OSTTRA services, but also directly through operational efficiency improvements and cost reductions for many of the largest banks in the world.\n\n   \u2022 Actively contribute to the development and architecture of the system to meet new and changing business needs\n   \u2022 Ensure that non-functional requirements are established and met\n   \u2022 Be part of the team taking care of the overall system health\n   \u2022 Engage in continuous learning to keep up with industry best practices\nWhat\u2019s in it for you:\n   \u2022 Influence the future of a market-leading solution together with highly skilled people across the globe\n   \u2022 Work in an empowered engineering team with people that want you to succeed\n   \u2022 Learn about the financial industry and contribute to the stability of the global financial system\n   \u2022 Expand your technical skill set by working in a modern tech stack\nWhat we\u2019re looking for:\nFundamental requirement:\n   \u2022 A master\u2019s degree in computer science or a similar field\n   \u2022 Around 5 years of relevant experience\n   \u2022 Excellent communication skills (fluency in English is a must)\n   \u2022 A bold and humble team player\n   \u2022 A desire to work in a modern tech stack including, but not limited to Python, TypeScript, React, NoSQL\/SQL databases, Docker and Kubernetes\n   \u2022 Business mindedness and a solution-oriented mindset\n   \u2022 An aptitude and willingness to improve yourself, others around you and our ways of working.\n\n Additional preferred requirements:\n   \u2022 An interest in financial markets\n   \u2022 A passion for technology\nThe location: Stockholm, Sweden\nRight to work requirements:\nThis role is limited to persons with right to work in the Sweden.\nCompensation\/benefits information: (This section is only applicable to US candidates)\nThe anticipated base salary range for this position is $A to $Z. Final base salary for this role will be based on the individual\u2019s geographic location, experience level, skill set, training, licenses and certifications.\nOur Benefits: Global vision, local impact\nAt OSTTRA, our benefits philosophy offers a market-competitive package that reflects our position as an industry leader. We want to ensure you feel valued, secure, and empowered wherever you are in the world.\nOur approach is built on three core pillars:\n   \u2022 Global foundations: We provide a baseline of excellence across all our offices, focusing on comprehensive Health & Wellness, Financial Security, and Work-Life Balance. No matter your location, you are part of a culture that prioritizes your holistic well-being.\n   \u2022 Locally tailored: We benchmark in each market to ensure our packages are genuinely competitive where you live and work.\n   \u2022 Flexibility and growth: We empower you to work in a way that suits your life. This includes a hybrid working model, generous leave policies, and a commitment to your continuous professional development.\n\nThe Trust employee ownership plan\nEvery employee at OSTTRA is an owner, and a member of The Trust, our employee ownership programme. Our distinct culture encourages colleagues to think and act like owners and raise the bar constantly.\nThis plan reflects our belief that when we work together to build a stronger, more valuable organisation, then all colleagues should benefit from the value we create.\nAbout OSTTRA\n\nWe build and operate the infrastructure that the world\u2019s post-trade financial system runs on. Launched in 2021, we have unified more than 20 years of heritage and expertise from four industry leaders into a single, integrated business.\nToday,we operate a trusted network that connects thousands of market participants to streamline end-to-end workflows, from trade capture through portfolio optimisation.We translate industry change into workable process, engineering an open, intelligent ecosystem that removes friction and reduces risk for the global markets.\n\nOur distinct ownership culture is underpinned by four behaviours: boldness, curiosity, accountability, and collaboration. In 2025 we were acquired by KKR, one of the world\u2019s most successful private equity firms, and are on a journey of growth and impact.\nJoining our team now is a unique opportunity - you will help to shape the next generation of post-trade, transform shared infrastructure into shared benefit, and accelerate your own career. Learn more at www.osttra.com.\nEqual opportunity employer statement at OSTTRA:\nWe are committed to fostering a connected and engaged workplace where all colleagues have access to opportunities based on their skills, experience, and contributions. Our hiring practices emphasise fairness, transparency, and merit, ensuring that we attract and retain the best talent. By valuing different perspectives and promoting a culture of respect and collaboration, we drive and operate the infrastructure that the world\u2019s post-trade financial system runs on.","ClientSiteName":"Client Careers Site","ClientSiteXRefCode":"CANDIDATEPORTAL","CompanyName":"OSTTRA","ParentCompanyName":"OSTTRA","JobDetailsUrl":"https:\/\/jobs.dayforcehcm.com\/en-US\/osttrahcm\/CANDIDATEPORTAL\/jobs\/1245","ApplyUrl":"https:\/\/jobs.dayforcehcm.com\/en-US\/osttrahcm\/CANDIDATEPORTAL\/jobs\/1245\/apply","City":"Stockholm","State":"Stockholm County","Country":"SE","PostalCode":"","JobFamily":"Technology","DatePosted":"2026-10-02T00:00:00","LastUpdated":"2026-10-02T14:43:35.53","ReferenceNumber":1245,"CultureCode":"en-US","ParentRequisitionCode":283,"JobType":0,"TravelRequired":0,"IsVirtualLocation":false},{"Title":"Cloud Engineer","Description":"Job Overview\n\n\nAbout the Role:\nThe team:\nSitting within OSTTRA's Technology and Infrastructure group, the Cloud Engineering team manages and optimizes the company-wide AWS and GCP workloads. We bridge the gap between Dev, Sec, and Ops by embedding robust DevSecOps methodologies and leveraging Infrastructure as Code (IaC) to drive infrastructure reliability, security, and velocity across the organization.\n\nResponsibilities and impact:\nWe are seeking a visionary and highly skilled Cloud Engineer with a minimum of 12 years of industry experience to join our cloud engineering team at Osttra. In this senior role, you will not just manage but take absolute ownership of our cloud infrastructure, deployment automation, and system reliability strategy.\nThe ideal candidate treats infrastructure completely as code, possesses a masterful understanding of container orchestration, and thrives on leading initiatives independently from conception to execution. You will be responsible for scaling our enterprise AWS environment, designing next-generation container ecosystems, and driving architectural consistency using Terraform and Terragrunt, while keeping an eye toward emerging technologies and AI-driven efficiencies\nKey Responsibilities\nTechnical Leadership & Initiative Ownership\n   \u2022 Lead Initiatives Independently: Take complete ownership of the DevOps roadmap, transforming high-level business goals into scalable, reliable platform architecture without requiring daily oversight.\n   \u2022 Architect Enterprise Infrastructure: Design, provision, and maintain secure, multi-tenant, high-availability AWS cloud infrastructure capable of supporting enterprise-scale workloads.\n   \u2022 Advanced Infrastructure as Code (IaC): Architect global, multi-region configurations using Terraform and Terragrunt to enforce a strict DRY (Don't Repeat Yourself) approach across complex, multi-account environments.\n   \u2022 Security & Governance: Define and implement enterprise-grade IAM frameworks, advanced network topologies (VPCs, Transit Gateways), and robust secrets management strategies.\nContainerization, Orchestration & Multi-Cloud Direction\n   \u2022 Kubernetes Mastery: Own the lifecycle, long-term scaling, and performance optimization of production-grade Amazon EKS clusters.\n   \u2022 Hybrid\/Multi-Cloud Expansion: Evaluate, design, and drive standardizations for alternative container platforms, heavily leveraging OpenShift or Google Cloud Platform (GCP) where business workflows demand hybrid or multi-cloud flexibility.\n   \u2022 Packaging & Scaling: Oversee complex application packaging via Helm, optimizing density and performance through advanced scheduling, autoscaling (HPA\/VPA), and cluster mesh topologies.\nCI\/CD, GitOps & Technical Exploration\n   \u2022 Enterprise CI\/CD Pipelines: Design and optimize secure, matrixed continuous integration and deployment workflows using GitHub Actions, ensuring native integration of automated security scanning (SAST\/DAST) and compliance testing.\n   \u2022 GitOps Advocacy: Drive organizational adoption of GitOps practices (e.g., ArgoCD or Flux) to treat git repositories as the absolute source of truth.\n   \u2022 Innovation & AI Adaptation: Bring a naturally curious mindset to the team. Actively explore, evaluate, and pioneer the adaptation of AI\/LLM developer tools (e.g., Gemini AI, automated IaC code generators, or AI-driven log anomaly detection) to maximize engineering velocity and optimize workflows.\nObservability & Site Reliability Engineering (SRE)\n   \u2022 Proactive SRE Culture: Elevate our enterprise observability stacks to focus on proactive anomaly detection and business-critical SLIs\/SLOs.\n   \u2022 Incident Post-Mortems: Guide engineering teams through high-severity incident response, leading comprehensive root-cause analyses (RCAs) that yield permanent structural remediations.\n   \u2022 Financial Operations (FinOps): Establish and execute sophisticated cloud cost-optimization strategies to maximize ROI without compromising performance.\n\nWhat we\u2019re looking for:\nRequired Skills & Qualifications\n   \u2022 Experience: 12+ years of dedicated experience in DevOps, Cloud Architecture, Platform Engineering, or Site Reliability Engineering (SRE) roles, with a proven track record of operating independently at a senior or staff level.\n   \u2022 Cloud Platform: Comprehensive, production-level mastery of Amazon Web Services (AWS) and its deep ecosystem (EC2, EKS, S3, RDS, IAM, Route53, Transit Gateway).\n   \u2022 Infrastructure as Code: Expert-level proficiency with Terraform and advanced hands-on experience using Terragrunt to manage complex enterprise infrastructure.\n   \u2022 Orchestration: Deep administration skills in Docker and Kubernetes (EKS).\n   \u2022 CI\/CD & Scripting: Proven experience building complex automated workflows in GitHub Actions, backed by strong scripting capabilities in Python and Bash.\n   \u2022 Soft Skills: A natural mentor with exceptional communication skills, capable of bridging gaps between software development, security, and product teams to drastically improve the developer experience.\nPreferred & Add-On Qualifications\n   \u2022 Enterprise Orchestration Add-on: Direct experience architecting and managing enterprise clusters using Red Hat OpenShift.\n   \u2022 Multi-Cloud Add-on: Production-level experience or certifications in Google Cloud Platform (GCP).\n   \u2022 Curiosity & AI Mindset: Demonstrated experience or personal curiosity exploring AI adaptation within infrastructure management, orchestration, or automated operations.\n   \u2022 Certifications (Highly Valued):\n         \u25e6 Certified Kubernetes Administrator (CKA) or Certified Kubernetes Security Specialist (CKS).\n         \u25e6 AWS Certified Solutions Architect \u2013 Professional or AWS Certified DevOps Engineer \u2013 Professional.\n         \u25e6 HashiCorp Certified: Terraform Authoring \/ Operations professional.\n\n\nThe location: Gurgaon,India","ClientSiteName":"Client Careers Site","ClientSiteXRefCode":"CANDIDATEPORTAL","CompanyName":"OSTTRA","ParentCompanyName":"OSTTRA","JobDetailsUrl":"https:\/\/jobs.dayforcehcm.com\/en-US\/osttrahcm\/CANDIDATEPORTAL\/jobs\/1247","ApplyUrl":"https:\/\/jobs.dayforcehcm.com\/en-US\/osttrahcm\/CANDIDATEPORTAL\/jobs\/1247\/apply","City":"Gurugram","State":"HR","Country":"IN","PostalCode":"","JobFamily":"Technology","EmploymentIndicator":"Regular","DatePosted":"2026-10-05T20:30:00","LastUpdated":"2026-10-06T12:26:17.337","ReferenceNumber":1247,"CultureCode":"en-US","ParentRequisitionCode":169,"JobType":0,"TravelRequired":0,"IsVirtualLocation":false},{"Title":"Apprentice TOC Monitoring Engineer","Description":"Job Overview\n\n\nAbout the Role:\nThe team:\nTOC Monitoring Team is a 24\/7 operational team that provides first-level technical support across all application and infrastructure alerts. Utilizing tools like Grafana and TOC OBS, the team proactively detects issues, manages application access, and resolves initial alerts around the clock. Our work helps to ensure continuous platform availability, seamless access management, and uninterrupted operations.\n\nResponsibilities and impact:\nWe are seeking a highly motivated and disciplined individual to join our Technical Operations Center (TOC) team as an Apprentice (Intern) TOC Engineer ( Monitoring). This is an entry-level position for a fresher providing foundational experience in a mission-critical 24x7 support environment. The primary responsibility is to be the first line of defense, monitoring key systems, identifying anomalies, and ensuring prompt escalation.\nKey Responsibilities\n\n   \u2022 24x7 Monitoring: Actively monitor multiple internal and client-facing applications, infrastructure, and services using various enterprise monitoring tools (e.g., Grafana, Monolith, etc.).\n   \u2022 Alert Triage & Initial Analysis: Acknowledge, categorize, and perform initial triage of all incoming alerts and incidents.\n   \u2022 Incident Logging: Accurately log all events and incidents in the ticketing system (Jira), ensuring comprehensive details are captured for escalation.\n   \u2022 Escalation Management: Follow established Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs) to escalate issues to the appropriate L2\/L3 teams, Subject Matter Experts (SMEs), or development teams within defined SLAs.\n   \u2022 Documentation: Maintain and update runbooks and knowledge base articles related to monitoring procedures and common alerts.\n   \u2022 Shift Handoffs: Clearly and concisely communicate all active issues, pending tasks, and recent activity during shift changes.\n\nWhat we\u2019re looking for:\n   \u2022 Education: Fresh graduate (or final-year student) in a technical discipline (e.g., B.Tech, MCA, or equivalent).\n   \u2022 Availability: Must be willing and able to work a flexible 24x7 shift rotation, including nights, weekends, and holidays.\n   \u2022 Technical Aptitude: A strong interest in IT infrastructure, networking, and application support.\n   \u2022 Communication: Excellent written and verbal communication skills to clearly convey technical issues.\n   \u2022 Discipline: High level of discipline and attention to detail required for following strict operational procedures.\n   \u2022 Preferred (But not required): Basic knowledge of Linux\/Unix command line or network concepts (TCP\/IP).\n\n\nThe location: Gurgaon,India\n\nOur Benefits: Global vision, local impact\nAt OSTTRA, our benefits philosophy offers a market-competitive package that reflects our position as an industry leader. We want to ensure you feel valued, secure, and empowered wherever you are in the world.\nOur approach is built on three core pillars:\n   \u2022 Global foundations: We provide a baseline of excellence across all our offices, focusing on comprehensive Health & Wellness, Financial Security, and Work-Life Balance. No matter your location, you are part of a culture that prioritizes your holistic well-being.\n   \u2022 Locally tailored: We benchmark in each market to ensure our packages are genuinely competitive where you live and work.\n   \u2022 Flexibility and growth: We empower you to work in a way that suits your life. This includes a hybrid working model, generous leave policies, and a commitment to your continuous professional development.\n\n\nThe Trust employee ownership plan\nEvery employee at OSTTRA is an owner, and a member of The Trust, our employee ownership programme. Our distinct culture encourages colleagues to think and act like owners and raise the bar constantly. This plan reflects our belief that when we work together to build a stronger, more valuable organisation, then all colleagues should benefit from the value we create.\n\nAbout OSTTRA\nWe build and operate the infrastructure that the world\u2019s post-trade financial system runs on. Launched in 2021, we have unified more than 20 years of heritage and expertise from four industry leaders into a single, integrated business.\nToday,we operate a trusted network that connects thousands of market participants to streamline end-to-end workflows, from trade capture through portfolio optimisation.We translate industry change into workable process, engineering an open, intelligent ecosystem that removes friction and reduces risk for the global markets.\nOur distinct ownership culture is underpinned by four behaviours: boldness, curiosity, accountability, and collaboration. In 2025 we were acquired by KKR, one of the world\u2019s most successful private equity firms, and are on a journey of growth and impact.\nJoining our team now is a unique opportunity - you will help to shape the next generation of post-trade, transform shared infrastructure into shared benefit, and accelerate your own career. Learn more atwww.osttra.com.\n\nEqual opportunity employer statement at OSTTRA\nWe are committed to fostering a connected and engaged workplace where all colleagues have access to opportunities based on their skills, experience, and contributions. Our hiring practices emphasise fairness, transparency, and merit, ensuring that we attract and retain the best talent. By valuing different perspectives and promoting a culture of respect and collaboration, we drive and operate the infrastructure that the world\u2019s post-trade financial system runs on.","ClientSiteName":"Client Careers Site","ClientSiteXRefCode":"CANDIDATEPORTAL","CompanyName":"OSTTRA","ParentCompanyName":"OSTTRA","JobDetailsUrl":"https:\/\/jobs.dayforcehcm.com\/en-US\/osttrahcm\/CANDIDATEPORTAL\/jobs\/1249","ApplyUrl":"https:\/\/jobs.dayforcehcm.com\/en-US\/osttrahcm\/CANDIDATEPORTAL\/jobs\/1249\/apply","City":"Gurugram","State":"HR","Country":"IN","PostalCode":"","JobFamily":"Technology","EmploymentIndicator":"Apprenticeship","DatePosted":"2026-10-06T20:30:00","LastUpdated":"2026-10-07T12:32:03.76","ReferenceNumber":1249,"CultureCode":"en-US","ParentRequisitionCode":290,"JobType":0,"TravelRequired":0,"IsVirtualLocation":false}];
                </script>

            
        </div>

    </section>

</div>


<style>
    .job_listing36 {
        background-color: ;
    }

    /* Job Card */

    .job_listing36 .job-card {
        transition: transform 0.2s ease, box-shadow 0.2s ease;
    }

    /* Job Title */

    .job_listing36 .job-card .card-title {
        font-size: 1.1rem;
        font-weight: 600;
        margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    }

    .job_listing36 .job-card .card-title a {
        color: #212222 !important;
        display: -webkit-box;
        -webkit-line-clamp: 2;
        -webkit-box-orient: vertical;
        overflow: hidden;
        min-height: calc(1.4em * 2);
    }

    .job_listing36 .job-card .card-title a:hover {
        color: #E73363 !important;
    }

    /* Job Meta (Location) */

    .job_listing36 .job-card .job-location.text-muted {
        font-size: 0.9rem;
    }

    /* Job Function Badge */

    .job_listing36 .job-card .badge {
        font-size: 0.75rem;
        padding: 0.4em 0.6em;
        background-color: rgba(231, 51, 99, 0.1) !important;
        color: #E73363;
        font-weight: 600;
        border-radius: 999px;
        display: flex;
        align-items: center;
    }

    /* Job badges */
    .job_listing36 .job-badge {
        background-color: rgba(231, 51, 99, 0.1);
        color: #E73363;
        font-weight: 600;
    }

    .job_listing36 .job-badge-secondary {
        background-color: #f1f3f5;
        color: #495057;
        font-weight: 500;
    }

    /* Job Description */

    .job_listing36 .job-card .job-description {
        font-size: 0.95rem;
        line-height: 1.4;
        overflow: hidden;
        z-index: 1;
        position: relative;
        max-height: 190px;
    }

    .job_listing36 .job-card .job-description::before {
        background: linear-gradient(180deg, hsla(0, 0%, 100%, .5) 35%, hsla(0, 0%, 100%, .5) 0, #fff);
        content: "";
        position: absolute;
        width: 100%;
        height: 30%;
        bottom: 0;
        z-index: 2;
    }

    .job_listing36 .view-details-link {
        font-size: 0.85rem;
        font-weight: 600;
        color: #E73363;
        text-decoration: none;
    }

    .job_listing36 .view-details-link:hover {
        color: #E73363 !important;
    }

    .job_listing36 .job-section h6 {
        color: #1f1f1f;
        font-weight: 600;
    }

    .job_listing36 .job-section p {
        margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    }

    .job_listing36 .job-section ul {
        padding-left: 0.68rem;
        margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    }

    .job_listing36 .job-section li {
        margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
    }

    /* Apply Button */

    .job_listing36 .job-card .btn {
        background-color: #E73363;
        border-color: #E73363;
        color: #ffffff !important;
        font-weight: 600;
        border-radius: 999px;
        transition: background-color 0.2s ease, transform 0.2s ease;
        align-self: flex-start;
    }

    .job_listing36 .job-card .btn:hover,
    .job_listing36 .job-card .btn:focus,
    .job_listing36 .job-card .btn:active {
        background-color: #cf2d58;
        border-color: #cf2d58;
        color: #ffffff;
        transform: translateY(-1px);
    }

    .job_listing36 .job-card .btn:focus-visible {
        box-shadow: 0 0 0 0.2rem rgba(231, 51, 99, 0.4);
    }

    /* Icons inside job cards */
    .job_listing36 .job-card i.fa-solid,
    .job_listing36 .job-card i.fa-regular {
        font-size: 0.9em;
    }

    /* Filter Dropdowns */

    .job_listing36 input.job-search {
        height: 100%;
    }

    .job_listing36 .filter-dropdown {
        position: relative;
        height: 100%;
    }

    .job_listing36 .filter-toggle {
        width: 100%;
        height: 100%;
        background: #eeeeee;
        padding: 0.3rem 1rem;
        font-size: 0.9rem;
        text-align: left;
        cursor: pointer;
        border: none;
        display: flex;
        align-items: center;
        justify-content: space-between;
    }

    .job_listing36 .filter-toggle:focus {
        outline: none;
    }

    /* Dropdown menu */
    .job_listing36 .filter-menu {
        position: absolute;
        top: 100%;
        left: 0;
        right: 0;
        background: #eeeeee;
        padding: 0.75rem;
        display: none;
        z-index: 10;
        max-height: 240px;
        overflow-y: auto;
    }

    .job_listing36 .filter-dropdown.open .filter-menu {
        display: block;
    }

    .job_listing36 .filter-menu label:last-child {
        margin-bottom: 0;
    }

    /* Options */
    .job_listing36 .filter-option {
        display: flex;
        align-items: center;
        gap: 0.5rem;
        font-size: 0.9rem;
        cursor: pointer;
        padding: 0.25rem 0;
    }

    .job_listing36 .filter-option input {
        accent-color: #E73363;
    }

    /* Selected Filter Chips */

    .job_listing36 .selected-filters-inner {
        border-top: 1px solid #D6D7D9;
        padding-top: 1rem;
    }

    .job_listing36 .filter-chip {
        display: inline-flex;
        align-items: center;
        gap: 0.6rem;
        background-color: #eee;
        color: #E73363;
        padding: .6rem .8rem .6rem 0.8rem;
        font-size: 0.9rem;
        margin-right: 10px;
        margin-bottom: 10px;
    }

    .job_listing36 .filter-chip button {
        background: none;
        border: none;
        color: inherit;
        padding: 0;
        line-height: 1;
        cursor: pointer;
    }

    .job_listing36 .filter-chip button:hover {
        opacity: 0.7;
    }

    /* Search Input Icons */

    .job_listing36 .search-icon,
    .job_listing36 .search-loader {
        position: absolute;
        top: 50%;
        right: 1.7rem;
        transform: translateY(-50%);
        color: #6c757d;
        pointer-events: none;
    }

    .job_listing36 i.fa-magnifying-glass,
    .job_listing36 i.fa-circle-notch {
        font-weight: 500;
    }

    .job_listing36 i.fa-angle-down {
        font-weight: 100;
        font-size: x-large;
        color: #E73363;
    }

    .job_listing36 i.fa-xmark {
        font-size: medium;
    }

    @media (min-width: 1400px) {
        .job_listing36 i.fa-xmark {
            font-size: large;
        }
    }

    @media (max-width: 991px) and (min-width: 768px) {
        .job_listing36 i.fa-xmark {
            font-size: x-small;
        }

        .job_listing36 i.fa-angle-down {
            font-size: large;
        }

        .job_listing36 .job-card .job-description {
            max-height: 150px;
        }
    }

    .job_listing36 .search-icon,
    .job_listing36 .search-loader {
        transition: opacity 0.15s ease;
    }


    @media (max-width: 575px) {
        .job_listing36 .job-card .btn {
            font-size: 14px;
        }
    }

    /* Accessibility: Reduced motion */

    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {

        .job_listing36 .job-card,
        .job_listing36 .job-card:hover {
            transition: none;
            transform: none;
        }
    }

    /* Remove native search clear (×) icon */

    /* Chrome, Safari, Edge (WebKit/Blink) */
    .job_listing36 input[type="search"]::-webkit-search-cancel-button,
    .job_listing36 input[type="search"]::-webkit-search-decoration,
    .job_listing36 input[type="search"]::-webkit-search-results-button,
    .job_listing36 input[type="search"]::-webkit-search-results-decoration {
        -webkit-appearance: none;
        appearance: none;
        display: none;
    }

    /* Firefox */
    .job_listing36 input[type="search"] {
        appearance: textfield;
    }
</style>
<script>
    document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {

        const jobCards = Array.from(document.querySelectorAll('.job_listing36 .job-card'));
        const searchInput = document.querySelector('.job_listing36 .job-search');
        const searchIcon = document.querySelector('.job_listing36 .search-icon');
        const searchLoader = document.querySelector('.job_listing36 .search-loader');

        const selectedFiltersInner = document.querySelector('.job_listing36 .selected-filters-inner');


        function debounce(fn, delay = 300) {
            let timeout;
            return (...args) => {
                clearTimeout(timeout);
                timeout = setTimeout(() => fn.apply(this, args), delay);
            };
        }

        function startSearch() {
            searchIcon.classList.add('d-none');
            searchLoader.classList.remove('d-none');
        }

        function endSearch() {
            searchLoader.classList.add('d-none');
            searchIcon.classList.remove('d-none');
            renderSearchChip();
        }

        /* Debounced search handler */
        const debouncedSearch = debounce(() => {
            applyFilters();
            endSearch();
        }, 300);

        const filters = {
            country: new Set()
        };

        /* ----------------------------------------
           Utilities
        ---------------------------------------- */

        function uniqueValues(key) {
            return [...new Set(jobCards.map(card => card.dataset[key]).filter(Boolean))].sort();
        }

        function updateCount(dropdown, set) {
            const count = dropdown.querySelector('.filter-count');
            count.textContent = set.size ? `(${set.size})` : '';
        }

        /* ----------------------------------------
           Build dropdown options
        ---------------------------------------- */

        document.querySelectorAll('.job_listing36 .filter-dropdown').forEach(dropdown => {
            const key = dropdown.dataset.filter;
            const menu = dropdown.querySelector('.filter-menu');

            uniqueValues(key).forEach(value => {
                const id = `${key}-${value.replace(/\s+/g, '-').toLowerCase()}`;

                menu.insertAdjacentHTML('beforeend', `
                <label class="filter-option" for="${id}">
                    <input type="checkbox" id="${id}" value="${value}">
                    <span>${value}</span>
                </label>
            `);
            });

            menu.addEventListener('change', e => {
                const value = e.target.value;
                e.target.checked ?
                    filters[key].add(value) :
                    filters[key].delete(value);

                updateCount(dropdown, filters[key]);
                renderFilterChips();
                renderSearchChip();
                applyFilters();
            });
        });

        document.querySelectorAll('.job_listing36 .filter-menu').forEach(menu => {
            menu.addEventListener('click', e => {
                e.stopPropagation();
            });
        });


        /* ----------------------------------------
           Dropdown toggle logic
        ---------------------------------------- */

        document.querySelectorAll('.job_listing36 .filter-toggle').forEach(toggle => {
            toggle.addEventListener('click', e => {
                e.stopPropagation();

                const dropdown = toggle.parentElement;
                const isOpen = dropdown.classList.contains('open');

                closeAllDropdowns();

                if (!isOpen) {
                    dropdown.classList.add('open');
                }
            });
        });


        document.addEventListener('click', closeAllDropdowns);

        function closeAllDropdowns() {
            document.querySelectorAll('.job_listing36 .filter-dropdown.open')
                .forEach(d => d.classList.remove('open'));
        }

        /* ----------------------------------------
           Filtering logic
        ---------------------------------------- */

        function applyFilters() {
            const search = searchInput.value.toLowerCase();
            let visibleCount = 0;

            jobCards.forEach(card => {
                const title = card.dataset.title.toLowerCase();

                const matchesSearch = !search || title.includes(search);

                const matchesCountry =
                    filters.country.size === 0 ||
                    filters.country.has(card.dataset.country);

                const visible =
                    matchesSearch &&
                    matchesCountry;

                card.parentElement.style.display = visible ? '' : 'none';
                if (visible) visibleCount++;
            });

            toggleEmptyState(visibleCount);
        }


        function renderFilterChips() {
            selectedFiltersInner.innerHTML = '';

            Object.entries(filters).forEach(([key, set]) => {
                set.forEach(value => {
                    const chip = document.createElement('span');
                    chip.className = 'filter-chip';
                    chip.dataset.filter = key;
                    chip.dataset.value = value;

                    chip.innerHTML = `
                ${value}
                <button type="button" aria-label="Remove ${value}">
                    <i class="fa-light fa-xmark"></i>
                </button>
            `;

                    selectedFiltersInner.appendChild(chip);
                });
            });

        }

        selectedFiltersInner.addEventListener('click', e => {
            const btn = e.target.closest('button');
            if (!btn) return;

            const chip = btn.closest('.filter-chip');
            const {
                filter,
                value
            } = chip.dataset;

            if (filter === "search") {
                searchInput.value = "";
            } else {
                // Remove from filter state
                filters[filter].delete(value);

                // Uncheck corresponding checkbox
                const checkbox = document.querySelector(
                    `.job_listing36 .filter-dropdown[data-filter="${filter}"] input[value="${CSS.escape(value)}"]`
                );

                if (checkbox) checkbox.checked = false;

                const dropdown = document.querySelector(`.job_listing36 .filter-dropdown[data-filter="${filter}"]`);

                updateCount(dropdown, filters[filter]);
            }

            renderFilterChips();
            renderSearchChip();
            applyFilters();
        });

        function renderSearchChip() {
            const existing = selectedFiltersInner.querySelector('[data-filter="search"]');
            if (existing) existing.remove();

            const value = searchInput.value.trim();
            if (!value) return;

            const chip = document.createElement('span');
            chip.className = 'filter-chip';
            chip.dataset.filter = 'search';
            chip.innerHTML = `
        ${value}
        <button type="button" aria-label="Clear search">
            <i class="fa-light fa-xmark"></i>
        </button>
    `;
            selectedFiltersInner.prepend(chip);
        }

        /* ----------------------------------------
           Empty state
        ---------------------------------------- */

        function toggleEmptyState(count) {
            let empty = document.querySelector('.job_listing36 #jobs-empty');

            if (!empty) {
                empty = document.createElement('div');
                empty.id = 'jobs-empty';
                empty.className = 'text-center mt-4';
                empty.textContent = 'No jobs match your filters.';
                document.querySelector('.job_listing36 .job-posts-grid').appendChild(empty);
            }

            empty.style.display = count === 0 ? 'block' : 'none';
        }

        searchInput.addEventListener('input', () => {
            startSearch();
            debouncedSearch();
        });

    });
</script><div class="spacer37" style="background-color: #ffffff;">
